        atns-subcat:b7b5cd08-d283-583c-a41f-39a8ccf7f555 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "In 1996 the Shire of Broome together with the Rubibi Working Group, entered into a partnership to provide increased recognition of Aboriginal people, their culture and traditions, and to incorporate these experiences and factors into the development, management and decision making process for the Broome area."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:17d993e0-d19e-5349-a48e-4de57b1dba59,
        atns-sub:5996de0c-8cc6-5f14-8901-d839af36a4d4,
        atns-sub:746b3b59-88ea-5685-81f7-1558875d7c47,
        atns-sub:7cc37d9a-fe3c-5fec-b115-d1bb8d72db9c,
        atns-sub:8ba4812a-c06b-587d-b491-67362ac3f001,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Broome, Western Australia, Australia"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=407> ;
    schema:name "Rubibi Interim Agreement with the Shire of Broome (1 May 1996)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "1996-05-01"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Since the interim agreement was signed, work has progressed on its implementation. The key to resolving disputes over land use has been through the town planning process. A study including intensive and wide public consultation has seen a broad overview developed for land use in Broome. This outcome will provide the framework for the next town planning scheme.

Since signing the Agreement the Rubibi Working Group and the Shire of Broome have embarked upon a partnership project, entitled: 'Town Planning for Aboriginal Culture and Heritage'. This project is funded by the Commonwealth Government under the Local Government Development Program and is intended to run for 12 months."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/agreements/files/Rubibi/RUBIAGRE.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

