idn-resource:06762685-07bb-54e8-aa06-6ee33f9df983 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007555"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7555"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:caa3eeb7-4d71-505c-9ee9-19b8c5338435 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """Doyle on behalf of the Iman People #2 v State of Queensland [2016] FCA 743.

Between: Richard Doyle, Patrick Silvester, Kenny Waterton, Eve Fesl, Eddy Waddy, Graham Anderson, Arwa Waterton, Cynthia Kemp, Bradley Curtis, Dena Marie Dodd-Ugle, Heidi Ann-Marie Lawson, Stuart White, Jason Jarro And Bevan Tull on behalf of The Iman People #2 (Applicants) and the State Of Queensland, the Banana Shire Council, the Central Highlands Council and others named in the Schedule (Respondents)

Judge: Reeves J.

Where made: Taroom, Queensland

Determination: Native title is held by the Iman People and exists within the entire determination area.

The Wardingarri Aboriginal Corporation holds the Iman People's native title rights and interests in trust.

Access to the full text of the determination is available via the URL link above."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:17d993e0-d19e-5349-a48e-4de57b1dba59,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7555> ;
    schema:name "Doyle on behalf of the Iman People #2 v State of Queensland [2016] FCA 743."@en ;
    schema:startDate "2016-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The Iman People hold native title over the entire determination area of approximately 498,804 hectares. Exclusive native title is held over approximately 475 hectares and non-exclusive native title is held over approximately 498,329 hectares.

The area is located in and around the town of Taroom, in Central South Western Queensland.

Details of Judgment

Reeves J. noted that the Iman People had provided extensive evidence in relation to their connection to each other and of their enduring relationship with the land and waters of the determination area [22] - [29].

Determination:

The Iman People #2's native title is recognised to exist over the whole of the determination area.

Exclusive native title

Exclusive native title rights and interests, other than in relation to water, exist over the areas described in Part 1 of Schedule 1 of the Federal Court of Australia (the FCA) determination.

Non-exclusive native title

Non-exclusive native title exists in relation to the land and waters in the areas described in Part 2 of Schedule 1 of the FCA determination. Those rights and interests include rights to access, camp, use and share or exchange natural resources for non-commercial purposes, conduct ceremonies, light fires, maintain and protect areas of significance.

Non-exclusive native title rights and interests exist in relation to parts of the township of Taroom, as described in Part 3 of Schedule 1 of the FCA determination. Those rights and interests include rights to access, fish and gather on the land and waters, maintain and protect areas of significance.

Non-exclusive native title rights and interests exist in relation to parts of the township of Wandoan, as described in Part 4 of Schedule 1 of the FCA determination. Those rights and interests include rights to access, hunt, fish, gather, use and share natural resources for non-commercial purposes, conduct ceremonies, maintain and protect areas of significance.

Non-native title interests

Non-native title interests within the determination area are listed in Schedule 4 of the FCA determination. Those interests include the interests of parties to the following agreements:

• Santos, Petronas and Iman People #2 GLNG ILUA (QI2010/10);

• Australia Pacific and Iman People ILU (QI2011/025);

• APLNG and Iman People Fairview and Eurombah Creek Projects ILUA (QI2013/032);

• ATP701P CSG ILUA (QI2002/044); - Iman People and LOcal Government ILUA (QI2015/012);

• Iman People #2 Comely and Mapala ILUA;

• Iman People #2 Coorada ILUA; - Iman People #2 Glenleigh ILUA;

• Iman People #2 Korcha ILUA; - Iman People #2 Woodine ILUA;

• Nathan Dam, Glebe Weir Raising and Pipelines Project ILUA;

• Wandoan and Taroom ILUA; and

• Iman People #2 QUD 6162/1998 and Ergon Energy Corporation Limited ACN 087 646 062.

To the extent that any of the non-native title interests contained in Schedule 4 of the FCA determination are inconsistent with the exercise of the native title then the native title has no effect but continues to exist for as long as the other interests exist."""@en ;
    schema:url "https://www.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/viewdoc/au/cases/cth/FCA/2016/743.html?context=1;query=Iman%20People%20#2;mask_path=au/cases/cth/FCA"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:067d978f-eaec-5514-a7eb-523153b1341a a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007639"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7639"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Port Curtis Coral Coast People and Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) between:

• Kerry Blackman, Dean Sarra, Lurleen Blackman, Richard Johnson, Nat Minniecon, Matthew Cooke and Neville Johnson on behalf of the Port Curtis Coral Coast People;

• Bundaberg Regional Council;

• North Burnett Regional Council;

• Gladstone Regional Council; and

• Gidarjil Cultural Heritage Corporation.

The application area covers about 18358 sq km, approx. 40 km south of Rockhampton extending south until approx. 18km north of Childers.

The purpose of the agreement is to provide agreement between the parties in relation to various high and low native title impact activities which can be undertaken on the land and waters within the native title claimant area.

The Native Title Representative Body for the area is Queensland South Native Title Services Ltd."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7639> ;
    schema:name "Port Curtis Coral Coast People and Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2016-045> ;
    schema:startDate "2016-09-22"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement:

The agreement took effect as a contractually binding agreement between the parties when the last party signed on 22 September 2016.

Termination:

The agreement continues indefinitely until terminated. The Extract contains no statement in relation to how the agreement may be treminated.

Native Title provisions:

Right to negotiate:The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993(Cth) do not apply to any 'future acts' covered by the agreement.

Extinguishment:

Schedule 8 of the agreement (High Native Title Imact Activities) notes that any activity which effects native title is temporray, undertaken for reasons of public health or safety, done persuant to a permitted lease, or required by law.

Future acts provisions:

The parties agree that the low native title impact activities, as outlined in Schedule 7 of the agreement, can be undertaken without conditions in relation to consent.

The parties consent to the high native title impact activities, as outlined in Schedule 8 of the agreement, only where the local government:

• has given notice to the Native Title Party, or their representative, and have completed consultations in accordance with the procedures set out in the agreement; or

• if the activity involves a capital work dealt with at a Capital Works Forum, then the local government provides a list of capital works in relation to the activity and consensus is reached about the activity being carried out in accordance with the procedures set out in the agreement.

Gladstone Regional Council and the Native Title Party have consented to a number of particular future acts which are subject to the following Native Title Acquisitions Agreements that meet the full and final satisfaction of any compensation and benefit of all Native Title Holders:

• the agreement dated 25 March 2013 in regard to Lot 41 SP206868 (Agnes Waters water treatment plant); and

• the agreement dated 11 July 2014 in regard to Lot 8 SP273519 (Calliope kindergarten); and Lots 206-214 on CP U7251 (Ubobo residential).

Native Title in the Area

This agreement is within the area of native title recognised in the Federal Court of Australia (FCA) proceeding Blackman & Ors on behalf of the Balai, Gurang, Gooreng, Taribelang Bunda People (FCA File No.: QUD6026/2001; NNT File No.: QCD2017/010). The First Nations Ballai, Gurang, Taribelang Bunda People Aboriginal Corporation holds the native title rights and interests in trust."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2016/045"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:067e6a3b-b8fb-5d92-bfdc-113c82123e5f a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:7b928a0d-47c5-537a-9136-066ae7f542f4 ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
