idn-resource:16eec597-fef8-5dd5-bfd4-d2d84290b0eb a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A004845"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "4845"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The BGP Douglas North Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)was agreed between the Power and Water Corporation (APPLICANT) and Arthur Que Noy, Gabriel Hazelbane, Paddy Huddlestone, Margaret Foster, Nothern Land Council, APT Bonaparte Pty Ltd, and BGP Tenure Holdings Pty Ltd (BGPT).

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for the construction and operation of a gas pipeline between Wadeye and Ban Ban Springs and for other acts necessary to give effect to this project."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:81edd075-cb8e-5a7e-a65d-a47cec815898,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=4845> ;
    schema:name "BGP Douglas North Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2009-03-05"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The parties consent to:
•the construction and operation of a gas pipeline between Wadeye and Ban Ban Springs;
•the grant and/or renewal of any assignment, transfer or substitution of any licence to permit the construction and commissioning of the pipeline within the ILUA area to the the Pipeline proponent or BGPT;
•the grant and/or renewal of any assignment or transfer of a non-exclusive tenure for the construction, commissioning, operation and maintenance of the pipeline; and
•to any and all acts necessary or incidental to the efficient implementation of the project provided that such acts have no greater effects on native title than any of the acts done in accordance with the grants and/or renewal expressly consented to in the ILUA.

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply, as the alternative consultation provisions are to be followed instead.

Without this agreement, the grant would have been invalid and the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) would apply. Under this Act any activity, such as a grant of land, that may affect native title rights is defined as a 'future act' and must comply with the future act provisions of the Act in order to be valid.

The ILUA is to operate 'for the duration of the project'."""@en .

idn-resource:16f43ef8-f691-5656-8be8-1af4ba78b9d2 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006555"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6555"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Yulluna People and Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between:

- Boulia Shire Council, Cloncurry Shire Council and McKinlay Shire Council;

- Brian Sullivan, Valerie Punch, Hazel Sullivan, Stan Sullivan and Allan Naumann on their own behalf and on behalf of the Yulluna People #3; and

- Yulluna Aboriginal Corporation

on 18 July 2014.

The purpose of this Area Agreement is to set out a consultation protocol with government."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6555> ;
    schema:name "Yulluna People and Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2014-008> ;
    schema:startDate "2014-07-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

The ILUA was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT) on 18 July 2014.

The Extract specifies 2 February 2014 as the specific start date for the Agreement.

The Agreement takes effect from the date of Execution, being the date upon which the last party signs the Agreement.

The Agreement will continue as a contractually binding agreement unless terminated. The Extract does not provide further information regarding applicable termination processes.

Native Title Provisions

The Extract notes that Part 2 Division 3 Subdivision P of the Native Title Act, which concerns the right to negotiate, does not apply to any Future Acts covered by the Agreement.

The parties to the Agreement consent to the doing of Low Impact Native Title Impact activities, including any activity involving construction and ground disturbing activity, action, undertaking, dealing, grant, approval,
consent and agreement.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Agreement Area includes all land and waters within the Native Title Determination Application QUD189/2010 (Yulluna People, QC2010/001), as accepted for registration on 9 August 2013.

The Yulluna People’s Native Title Application QUD6012/99 was registered on 20th April 1999.
The claim area is approximately 3,392 square kilometres.

The Yulluna People #2 Native Title Application QUD6004/02 was registered on 5th July 2002.
The claim area is approximately 1,027 square kilometres."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2014/008"^^xsd:anyURI .

