    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Southwell Holding Native Title Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was signed to establish an arrangement of 'working co-existence' between native title parties, pastoral lessees and the government. It provides guidelines for the parties to arrange land access and to conduct activities under their respective titles, rights and interests in the ILUA area.

This ILUA has been registered in conjuction with the Wik & Wik-Way and Cook Shire Council ILUA and the Strathburn Holding and Holroyd River Holding Native Title Agreement ILUAs to bring into effect the Wik Peoples v State of Queensland [2004] FCA 1306 consent determination."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:078baf41-50e7-561d-9163-fb3b43a98261,
        atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:746b3b59-88ea-5685-81f7-1558875d7c47,
        atns-sub:9e5e8f61-69be-5e2a-a9cd-58fb000349bd,
        atns-sub:b9cb4d2e-5a5b-57ae-a2ac-5450c37a61d8,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Cape York Peninsula, Queensland, Australia"@en ;
