    schema:description "The Kluane First Nation Self-Government Agreement Implementation Plan was developed by the Kluane First Nation, the Government of Yukon and the Government of Canada. It was signed on 18 October 2003. Clause 23.1 of the Kluane First Nation Self-Government Agreement (the Self-Government Agreement) requires the establishment of an Implementation Plan which is to guide the implementation of that Agreement. The Implementation Plan sets out the obligations and activities of each of the parties to the Self-Government Agreement. The Implementation Plan does not create legal obligations beyond those contained in that Agreement."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:078baf41-50e7-561d-9163-fb3b43a98261,
        atns-sub:17d993e0-d19e-5349-a48e-4de57b1dba59,
        atns-sub:51ca8813-b7bb-5a37-819e-afae35771fff,
