    schema:name "KERG Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2002-05-17"^^xsd:date .

idn-resource:1a45ed4d-13c2-5e9e-9175-0529f657fd96 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:4568b733-fdfa-5fcf-9e0b-3a3bddf5077e ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:country atns-country:244f6961-729f-5b21-8fc9-baff9dd9af7e ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A002569"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "2653"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:1682bda6-86ad-57ab-b605-73fb7027939d ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Indigenous Community at Derby has signed two Shared Responsibility Agreements (SRAs) designed to strengthen families. The 'Family and Community Safety' SRA hopes to improve safety through an awareness campaign.

Shared Responsibility Agreements are agreements between governments and Indigenous communities to provide discretionary funding in return for community obligations. The new arrangements developed from an initiative of the Council of Australian Governments and replace the previous ATSIC system of funding. For more information see ‘Shared Responsibility Agreement’ below."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:5996de0c-8cc6-5f14-8901-d839af36a4d4,
        atns-sub:d15dd1de-4696-50c8-9f10-2e95eea88e6f,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Derby, Western Australia, Australia"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=2653> ;
    schema:name "Derby 'Family and Community Safety' Shared Responsibility Agreement (SRA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2005-03-22"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The Derby 'Family and Community Safety' SRA was signed by the Commonwealth Government and the Jayida Burru Forum, who acted as a representative of local community groups.

Purpose

The SRA provides a range of activities designed to improve family and community safety. These include awareness sessions on violence, practical workshops through TAFE and a local radio campaign.

Shared Responsibilities

The Commonwealth government will fund a coordinator for the activities listed above. The iniaitive 'Talk Up for You' will also be re-launched in schools. $60,000 has been allocated for this purpose.

The community at Derby has agreed to work together to develop 'new ideas for building family and community safety in a culturally appropriate way' (SRA Fact Sheet). Under the SRA, the community agrees to participate in activities and attend counselling sessions where appropriate.

The Derby SRAs are administered by the Derby Indigenous Coordination Centre."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.indigenous.gov.au/sra/search/document.aspx?id=8154"^^xsd:anyURI .

