idn-resource:1a890ae3-761a-53b6-8b22-6f974f5b4098 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A005650"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "5650"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """This agreement is an Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) between:

- Billy Atkins, Miriam Atkins, Slim Williams, Kate George, Stan Hill and Anthony Charles in their capacity as the registered native title claimant for the Gingirana People; and
- Sandfire Resources NL.

The purpose of this agreement is to secure a mining interest over the ILUA area for Sandfire Resources."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5650> ;
    schema:name "Gingirana People and Sandfire Resources Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2012-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

Commencement and Termination

The agreement came into effect on the day that the parties signed the agreement. This date has not been released, therefore it is uncertain when the agreement became active. The agreement will continue for as long as Sandfire Resources has an interest in any Mining Tenement or Ancillary Title in the ILUA Area. However, this agreement can be terminated by the agreement of the parties, recorded in writing.

Future Acts

The parties agreed to a number of future acts, subject to the compliance by the parties with the ILUA and also the agreement entitled "Gingirana LAA (with provision for an ILUA)" and dated 18 November 2010.

These future acts generally relate to the granting of a Mining Tenement or Ancillary Title to Sandgate Resources. Grant is used in broad sense and covers a grant, renewal, amalgamation or variation. Specific future acts are listed in Schedule B.

Right to Negotiate

The Right to Negotiate as expressed in Part 2, Division 3, Subdivision P of the Native Title Act does not apply any future act.

Background

Sandfire Resources' Doolgunna Copper-Gold Project is located 900km north of Perth and approximately 150km north of Meekatharra, Western Australia. The project area lies close to a number of existing and historical gold mines and infrastructure including the Goldfields Gas Pipeline and Great Northern Highway. Within the Doolgunna project operates a secondary project, the DeGrussa Project. The area covered by this secondary project is the area which affects this ILUA.

To facilitate this Project Sandfire Resources have signed two ILUAs - this ILUA with the Gingirana People and an additional ILUA with the Yugunga Nya Native Title Claimant Group. These ILUA's have allowed for Sandfire Resources to be granted the necessary Mining Lease by the Western Australian Government to undertake activities in these areas.

The Yugunga-Nya ILUA resulted in both financial and non-financial benefits including employment and contracting opportunities. Such details have not been released with regards to this ILUA, however, it is likely that similar financial and non-financial benefits will result."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/WA_-_Registered_Ilua_-_Gingirana_People_and_Sandfire_Resources_Indigenous_Land_Use_Agreement_WI2011_009.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:1a8a7bc3-6d99-5a22-a1be-0d0ecc1efbfa a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A005914"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "5914"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Jangga/Wyarra (aka Why Not) Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between:

- Stephen John Plath and Jennifer Maria Plath (applicant); and

- Bulganunna Aboriginal Corporation

on 25 November 2013.

The purpose of this Body Corporate ILUA is to grant consent regarding pastoral activities within the Agreement Area."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5914> ;
    schema:name "Jangga/Wyarra (aka Why Not) Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2013-057> ;
    schema:startDate "2013-11-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

The ILUA was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT) on 25 November 2013.

The Extract does not specify specific start or end dates for the Agreement.

However, the Extract does note that the Agreement takes effect on the Date of Determination of Native Title in favour of the Jangga People, being 9 October 2012.

The Agreement will continue in effect until:

(a) the Lease term expires; or
(b) the date of surrender, resumption, forfeiture or termination of the Lease; or
(c) the date upon which the Agreement is removed from the Register of ILUAs.

The Extract does not include extensive information regarding the terms of the Agreement.

Native Title Provisions

The Extract notes that there are no statements within the Agreement of the kind which are mentioned in 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth).

This means that the ILUA does not:

- provide consent for the doing of any acts by
non-native title parties;

- effect the right of the native title parties to negotiate with non-native title parties proposing to undertake a future act; nor

- validate any previous future acts.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

On 9 October 2012, the Federal Court of Australia recognised the Jangga People’s Native Title rights and interests over approximately 11,350 square kilometres of land in Central Queensland. The decision of McLennan on behalf of the Jangga People v State of Queensland [2012] FCA 1082 effectively reaffirms the Jangga People’s affinity with their traditional lands around Mount Coolon, Urella and Lake Dalrymple."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2013/057"^^xsd:anyURI .

