    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Traveston Crossing Dam Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between Queensland Water Infrastructure Pty Ltd (QWI)(APPLICANT), Alex Bond, Bessie Bond, Alex Davidson, Barry Donas, Bill Glenbar, Lurlene Henderson, Lynette Johannessen, Andy Muckan, Melita Orcher and Edna Van Hemmen on their own behalf and on behalf of the Kabi Kabi People on 14 April 2008. The purpose of this ILUA is to provide for consent of the native title party to the grant of project rights for the planning, construction, operation, maintenance and ultimate decommissioning of the Traveston Crossing Dam.

The ILUA was registered on 14 April 2008, and ends on the earlier of either of QWI interests in the Project being surrendered, cancelled or discontinued or the decommissioning of the Traveston Crossing Dam and any required rehabilitation of the affected land."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
