idn-resource:21a32d5b-295a-57f8-979c-552c05e011ae a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007602"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7602"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Brooking Springs Station Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed under the Native Title Act 1993(Cth), between the Bunuba Dawangarri Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate ('RNTBC') and Kenneth Andrew Vivian as executor for the estate of Jillian Mary Jenyns.

The agreement area covers 1840.5 km, immediately north and west of Fitzroy Crossing Townsite, in the Kimberley region of Western Australia.

The purpose of the agreement is to allow access to the land and waters subject to the Brookings Springs Station Pastoral Lease."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7602> ;
    schema:name "Brooking Springs Station Indigenous Land Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2016-017> ;
    schema:startDate "2017-07-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Agreement Area:

The agreement area covers the land and waters of the Brooking Springs Station Pastoral Lease (N050174), as laid out in Annexure A of the agreement.

Commencement:

The agreement commences to the extent that the agreement has force as a contract on the date it is executed by all parties (not specified in the Extract). It has force as an Indigenous Land Use Agreement upon its registration.

Termination:

The agreement continues until: (a) the parties have no further rights or obligations under the agreement; or (b) the parties agre in writing to end it.

If requested by either party, the agreement is subject to review by the Pastoralists, the Bunuba Dawangarri Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC and the Bunuba People two years after the commencement date and every two years thereafter.

Native Title Provisions:

The Extract notes that there are no statements within the agreement of the kind which are mentioned in ss 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), and so the consequences set out under these sections are not triggered by this agreement. This means the agreement does not provide consent for the doing of any acts by non-native title parties; effect the right of the native title parties to negotiate with non-native title parties proposing to undertake a future act; nor validate any previous future acts.

Native Title the Agreement Area:

The agreement is located within the native title determination area of the Federal Court of Australia (FCA) proceeding Brooking on behalf of the Bunuba People (Bunuba #2) v State of Western Australia [2015] FCA 1481 (FCA file no.: WAD94/2012; NNTT file no.: WCD2015/009). By consent of the parties, it was determined that native title exists and is held by the Bunuba People over land and waters in the vicinity of Fitzroy Crossing in the Kimberley region of Western Australia. Exclusive and non-exclusive native title rights and interests were recognised, with the area of the Brooking Springs Station Pastoral Lease being an area of non-exclusivity."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2016/017"^^xsd:anyURI .

