idn-resource:23d141af-f7d6-541f-89c3-7251e232ba55 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007712"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7712"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Dauan Health Care Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between :

• the State of Queensland acting through the Torres and Cape Hospital and Health Service;

• Charles Bigie on his own behalf and on behalf of the Dauan People;

• the Dauanalgaw (Torres Strait Islanders) Corporation RNTBC; and

• the Torres Strait Island Regional Council.

The agreement area covers about 783 sq km, consisting of 3 lots on Dauan (Mt Cornwallis Island) in the Torres Strait.

The purpose of the agreement is to provide consent for the demolition of the Dauan Primary Health Care Centre and for the construction of new health care facilities.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Torres Strait Regional Authority."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:d15dd1de-4696-50c8-9f10-2e95eea88e6f,
        atns-sub:dc50c698-80b0-5ef4-bd95-928f2be8da05,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7712> ;
    schema:name "Dauan Health Care Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2018-026> ;
    schema:startDate "2019-03-06"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement:

The agreement commences on the date the agreement is executed by the parties, with the exception of clauses 6 and 9.1 which commence on 6 March 2019 (the registration date).

Termination:

The Extract does not contain any information regarding the termination of the agreement.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to the doing of the agreed acts (see below).

Extinguishment

The parties agree that the non-extinguishment principle applies - this means that under s 24EB (3) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) any of the activities authorised under this agreement which may be inconsistent with native title rights and interests do not extinguish these interests, instead they are revived when the activities are finished.

Future act provisions

This agreement provides consent for the doing of agreed acts, which are the demolition of the Dauan Primary Health Care Centre, the granting of short term and long term leases and the construction of new health care facilities, namely:

• the new Dauan Primary Health Care Centre and staff accommodation;

• a temporary Health Clinic;

• a construction lay down area; and

• any other new facilities to be constructed on the agreement area under the terms of the leases.

The agreement also provides consent for the doing of any future acts necessary or incidental to the above.

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The agreement is located within the area of native title recognised by the Federal Court of Australia in the consent determination proceeding Dauan People v State of Queensland [2000] FCA 1064 (FCA File No.: QUD6248/1998; NNTT File No. QCD2000/002)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2018/026"^^xsd:anyURI .

