    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Phillip Creek PPL Bulk Handling Facility ILUA was agreed between the Patta Warramungu People, the Central Land Council, Global Port Solution Pty Ltd and the Northern Territory of Australia. The purpose of the ILUA is to provide for the construction of a bulk handling facility by Global Port Solutions Pty Ltd."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5083> ;
    schema:name "Phillip Creek PPL Bulk Handling Facility Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2009-11-17"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The ILUA provides for the surrender and extinguishment of native title interests in the agreement area.

It provides for the grant of a Crown lease over the area with with attached development conditions over that area. If these conditions are met, the ILUA provides for a grant of a fee simple estate over the agreement area.

A bulk handling facility is to be constructed on the agreement area next to the Adelaide to Darwin Railway. The construction is to be undertaken by Global Port Solutions Pty Ltd.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The ILUA covers land over which the Patta Warumungu people established non-exclusive native title rights and interests in Patta Warumungu People v Northern Territory of Australia [2007] FCA 1386."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/ILUA%20Register/2009/DI2009.003/ILUARegisterExport.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

