idn-resource:2f90602f-5bae-5be5-a90a-7d34e882efe0 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A008021"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "8021"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Gulngay People Tenure Resolution Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA') was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between the State of Queensland and Gulngay Kinjufile Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate ('RNTBC').

The ILUA area covers about 6 sq km and includes multiple land parcels centered generally in the vicinity of Tully and extending approximately 24 km north, 15 km west, 17 km south east and 10 km north east.

The purpose of the agreement is the surrender of native title in revenue share lots and giving consent to agreed acts within the ILUA area.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the North Queensland Land Council Native Title Representative Body Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=8021> ;
    schema:name "Gulngay People Tenure Resolution Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2019-018> ;
    schema:startDate "2019-10-15"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Agreement area:

The ILUA area covers approx. 6 sq km and includes multiple land parcels centered generally in the vicinity of Tully and extending approx. 24 km northerly, 15 km westerly, 17 km south easterly and 10 km north easterly.

The Extract from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements identifies the area subject to this ILUA, per the lots included in Schedule 1 of the Agreement. For more information, see the documents attached below.

Commencement and Termination:

The agreement commenced on the date the agreement was signed by the last party. The ILUA came into force when the agreement was registered on 15 October 2019.

The agreement will continue in force unless terminated by written agreement signed by the parties.

The agreement may also be terminated by a determination of the Federal Circuit Court that native title does not exist in part of the agreement area, or a determination that native title is held by people other than the Gulngay People in part of the determination area. In such cases, the agreement will cease in that part of the agreement area but remain in force in relation to the remaining area.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate:

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to the acts consented to in this ILUA.

Extinguishment:

The Gulngay Kinjufile Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC surrenders all native title rights and interests in the surrender area. The surrender area is any revenue share lot in the ILUA area.

For all other agreed acts, the parties agree that the non-extinguishment principle applies, meaning that any acts authorised under this ILUA which may be inconsistent with native title rights and interests do not extinguish those rights and interests.

Future act provisions:

The parties consent to the doing of certain agreed acts, including:

• the surrender of all native title rights and interests to the state over the revenue share lots;

• the grant of any interest, including a permit, lease, easement or reserve for community purposes over any revenue share lot prior to the revenue share lot being granted in fee simple in accordance with the relevant requirements of the agreement;

• any grant of Aboriginal land over the ALA lots in accordance with the requirements of the agreement and the Aboriginal Land Act 1991 (Qld);

• the opening of any roads in accordance with clause 12 of the agreement;

• the creation of the reserves including the appointment of trustees in accordance with the requirements of the agreement;

• the inclusion of any area into the protected estate area in accordance with the requirements of the agreement, being those areas to which the Nature Conservation Act 1992 (Qld) applies;

Schedule 9 details all the agreed acts and is attached below.

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The ILUA area is within the area of the native title determination Kinjun on behalf of the Gulngay People v State of Queensland [2019] FCA 446. (FCA file no.:QUD308/2014, NNTT file no.: QCD2019/003)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2019/018"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:2f9b3348-d146-504a-90ad-482f9815355f a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A008709"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "8709"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Malgana Wooramel Pastoral Lease Agreement Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between Clausen Pty Ltd and the Malgana Aboriginal Corporation.

The purpose of the ILUA is to facilitate the Malgana People's access to approximately 358 square kms of the Carey Downs Lease area.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Yamatji Marlpa Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=8709> ;
    schema:name "Malgana Wooramel Pastoral Lease Agreement"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2020-019> ;
    schema:startDate "2020-12-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Background to the Agreement

This ILUA is within the native title area of the Malgana People, that was determined by consent in Oxenham on behalf of the Malgana People v State of Western Australia [2018] FCA 1929 (Malgana Part A). Clausen Pty Ltd was a respondent to the application for that determination.

Details of the Agreement

Commencement and Termination

The ILUA is binding from the date when signed by all the parties. This date is not included in the Extract. It has effect as an ILUA, and in relation to the agreed acts, from its registration date.

Native Title Provisions

Right to negotiate

The parties have agreed that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) (NTA) apply.

Extinguishment

The parties agree that the non-extinguishment principle applies - this means that under s 24EB(3) of the NTA, any of the activities authorised under this ILUA which may be inconsistent with native title rights and interests do not extinguish these rights and interests, instead they are revived when the activities are finished.

Future act provisions

The Extract notes that there are no statements within the ILUA of the kind which are mentioned in ss 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the NTA, and so the consequences set out under these sections are not triggered. This means that the ILUA does not: provide consent for the doing of any acts by non-native title parties; affect the right of the native title parties to negotiate with non-native title parties proposing to undertake a future act; nor validate any previous future acts.

Native Title in the Agreement Area

The ILUA area is within the area of the native title determination Oxenham on behalf of the Malgana People v State of Western Australia [2018] FCA 1929. (FCA file no.: WAD6236/1998, NNTT file no.: WCD2018/012)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2020/019"^^xsd:anyURI .

