    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Yellowknives Participation Agreement was developed to reflect and reinforce the principles of mutual respect, active partnership, and long term commitment that guide the working relationship between the Yellowknives Dene First Nation and Diavik Diamond Mines Inc. (DDMI) in the Diavik Diamonds Project."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:51ca8813-b7bb-5a37-819e-afae35771fff,
        atns-sub:5996de0c-8cc6-5f14-8901-d839af36a4d4,
        atns-sub:9073e633-80a9-5ba7-8892-f556bd0a0612,
        atns-sub:9e5e8f61-69be-5e2a-a9cd-58fb000349bd,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Northwest Territories, Canada"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=1861> ;
    schema:name "Yellowknives Kwe K'a Ndi Participation Agreement with Diavik Diamond Mines Inc."@en ;
    schema:startDate "2000-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The key undertakings in the Yellowknives Kwe K’a Ndi Participation Agreement provide for:
· DDMI’s commitments to provide employment and business opportunities to members of the Yellowknives Dene First Nation. To facilitate the achievement of these objectives, the Yellowknives Dene First Nation has agreed to maintain and make available to DDMI on an ongoing basis, an up-to-date human resource inventory and a business registry for their membership.
· The creation of a joint implementation committee to outline responsibilities, tasks and timelines for reaching project-related employment and business development targets for the Yellowknives Dene. The Yellowknives Dene First Nation agrees to employ a representative to liaise with DDMI on these and other social development issues.
· The affirmation by the Yellowknives Dene First Nation for its support for the development, construction and operations of the Diavik Diamonds Project as approved by the Federal Minister of the Environment in November 1999. In so providing, the Yellowknives Dene First Nation has expressed their intent to ratify the Diavik Environmental Agreement and the Socio-Economic Monitoring Agreement.

In addition to this agreement, DDMI has completed Participation Agreements with four other neighbouring Aboriginal groups including, the Lutsel K'e Dene Band, the Dogrib Treaty 11 Council, the North Slave Metis Alliance and the Kitikmeot Inuit Association."""@en .

idn-resource:3389c1f5-1fbd-595b-9878-4964147348f6 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A008007"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "8007"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Topsy Creek Barge Ramp Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA') was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between the Kowanyama Aboriginal Shire Council and the Abm Elgoring Ambung Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate ('RNTBC').

The agreement area covers about 0.4 hectares within Lot 20 on SP224321. It is located between the eastern bank of the Topsy Creek and the Topsy Road, about 7.2 km northwest of the town of Trebanaman.

The purpose of the agreement is to provide consent for the construction and establishment of the Barge Ramp on the eastern bank of the Topsy River.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Cape York Land Council Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=8007> ;
    schema:name "Topsy Creek Barge Ramp Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2018-001> ;
    schema:startDate "2018-01-22"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Agreement area:

The agreement area covers about 0.4 hectares within Lot 20 on SP224321. It is located between the eastern bank of the Topsy Creek and the Topsy Road, about 7.2 km northwest of the town of Trebanaman.

The Extract from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements identifies the area subject to this ILUA, per schedule 2 of the agreement, as part of Lot 20 on SP224321. For more information, see the documents attached below.

Commencement and Termination:

The agreement commenced on 22 January 2018 (the date that it had been signed by all the parties). It has effect as an ILUA from the date that it was entered onto the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements, 18 May 2018. The parties may end the ILUA by written agreement.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title act 1993 (Cth) apply to the acts agreed to under this ILUA.

Extinguishment

Any acts done by non-native title parties under this agreement will not extinguish native title rights and interests.

Future act provisions

The parties consent to any activities in relation to the construction and establishment of:

• the Barge Ramp and hardstand area;

• the surrender of the road opening area (shown as "New Road" on schedule 1 map);

• any other activity, including surveys, geotechnical investigations, grants of any authorisations including making a development application and approval, clearing land, and using the Topsy Turvy Bridge.

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The agreement is within the area of the Kowanyama People's native title recognised in the Federal Court of Australia ('FCA') proceeding Kowanyama People v State of Queensland [2009] FCA 1192 (FCA file no.: QUD6119/1998; NNTT file no.: QCD2009/003)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2018/001"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:339b8dc5-3233-5a73-b9ee-09d8c315cd2b a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007134"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7134"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """Budjiti People/Bundoona Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is an Area Agreement between:

- Bundoona Nominees Pty Ltd and Randal Kenneth Newsham (applicant); and

- Dinny McKellar, Phillip Eulo, Elizabeth McNiven, Margaret Hearn, Carolyn Hooper and Melissa Bryan on behalf of the Budjiti People.

The purpose of this Agreement is not specified within the ILUA Extract."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7134> ;
    schema:name "Budjiti People/Bundoona Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2015-027> ;
    schema:startDate "2015-11-23"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement

This ILUA was registered with the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements on 23 November 2015.

The Agreement Extract does not provide a specific start or end date for the Agreement.

The Agreement Extract does state however, that subject to clauses 5.4 and 5.5 of the Agreement, this Agreement is to take effect on the date that a determination of native title in favour of the Budjiti People is made.

It also states that subject to clauses 5.4 and 5.5 of the Agreement, this Agreement is to continue until:
- the date of expiry of the Lease term; or
- the date of surrender, resumption, forfeiture or termination of the Lease; or
- the date of removal of the Agreement from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements.

Native Title Provisions

The Agreement Extract states that the Agreement does not include any statements in respect of future acts whereby the right to negotiate applies, as mentioned in subs 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Agreement area falls within the Budjiti People native title application QUD53/2007.

In McKellar on behalf of the Budjiti People v State of Queensland [2015] FCA 601 the Federal Court of Australia determined that the Budjiti People hold non-exclusive native title rights and interests over the entire Determination Area."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2015/027"^^xsd:anyURI .

