idn-resource:351a5a72-90a8-5c53-80cb-94b5ce3231ea a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:4be1244b-2872-5199-8ba6-8c25fb02095d,
        idn-resource:688fb88a-9e86-545d-a101-1f81b1caeeb9 ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:country atns-country:244f6961-729f-5b21-8fc9-baff9dd9af7e ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A000195"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "560"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:caa3eeb7-4d71-505c-9ee9-19b8c5338435 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """Andrew Passi on behalf of the Meriam People v State of Queensland [2001] FCA 697

Between: Andrew Passi on behalf of the Meriam People (APPLICANT) AND
State of Queensland (RESPONDENT)

Judge: Chief Justice Black
Where: Dauar Island in the Torres Strait

Determination:
Native title exists in the determination area.

The area covered by the determination is shown on the Native Title Determination Plan Number AP5177 and includes the whole of the land and inland water of Waier Island and Dauar Island on the landward side of the high water mark."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:746b3b59-88ea-5685-81f7-1558875d7c47,
        atns-sub:9e5e8f61-69be-5e2a-a9cd-58fb000349bd,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Waier and Dauar Islands, Torres Strait, Queensland, Australia"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=560> ;
    schema:name "Andrew Passi on behalf of the Meriam People v State of Queensland [2001] FCA 697 (14 June 2001)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2001-06-14"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The Meriam People were the applicants in Mabo v Queensland [No 2] (1992) 175 CLR 1, however the land subject to this consent determination was expressly put to one side and excluded from the finding in that case. The original application to the National Native Title Tribunal was lodged on behalf of the Dauwereb People, a subgroup of the Meriam People, on 24 June 1998, shortly before amendments were made to the Native Title Act 1993 by the Native Title Amendment Act 1998. On 26 October the parties were referred by the Tribunal to mediation in accordance with the Native Title Act 1993. The mediation was successful and consequently Chief Justice Black made a consent determination finding that the Meriam people held native title. The native title is to be held on trust for the Meriam People by the Mer Gedkem Le (Torres Strait Islanders) Corporation.

The consent determination declared that the Meriam People were the common law holders of the land in the claim area. The communal and group rights and interests which comprise native title ensure the Meriam People may posses, occupy, use and enjoy the land to the exclusion of all others subject to their traditional laws and customs and the operation of valid laws of the Commonwealth and State of Queensland. The nature and extent of these rights was explored in further detail by Chief Justice Black in the consent determination. As with the majority of consent determinations, the orders were made in respect of land that was either unallocated crown land, reserved land or land already held by, or for the benefit of, Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander People. The claim related to two islands, Dauer and Waier, which were not permanently inhabited at that time but were deemed to have been ‘occupied’ for the purposes of the Native Title Act 1993 by Chief Justice Black.

Other interests in the area were recognised by the consent determination. They include the rights and interests of both Papua New Guinea and Australia in the claim area protected by the Treaty between Australia and the Independent State of Papua New Guinea concerning the area known as the Torres Strait, and Related Matters. The Crown and the State of Queensland also hold interests pursuant to any statute or valid executive or legislative act that was current at the date of this determination. The rights and interests of other parties prevail over the rights and interests of the native title holders when they cannot exist concurrently."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/disp.pl/au/cases/cth/federal%5fct/2001/697.html?query=title+%28+%22passi%22+%29"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:351b0650-22d9-5dca-8edf-62293b66797e a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007653"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7653"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Budina and Middalya Indigenous land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between Three Corners Properties Pty Ltd and the Budina Aboriginal Corporation.

The agreement area covers about 20 sq km, located about 230 km north-east of Carnarvon.

The purpose of the agreement is to consent to access, pastoral activities and low impact tourism in the Midalaya Pastoral Lease (N05022).

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Yamatji Marlpa Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:f630e08a-ea9c-57e3-ab87-066e4b9ad57e,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7653> ;
    schema:name "Budina and Middalya Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2017-020> ;
    schema:startDate "2018-05-03"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

Commencement:

The agreement has force as a contract upon its signing, and as an ILUA from the date of its registration, 3 May 2018.;

Termination:

The agreement, except for Clause 15 (Confidentiality), terminates when the Pastoral Lease comes to an end, or by the written agreement of all the parties.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate:

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) will not apply with respect to the agreed acts.

Future Act Provisions:

The Extract notes that there are statements within the agreement of the kind which are mentioned in ss24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), and so the consequences set out under those sections are triggered by this agreement. This means that the agreement provides consent for the doing of certain acts by non-native title parties. Specifically, this agreement provides the consent of the Budina Aboriginal Corporation and the Budina People for the doing of the following acts:

• the renewal, re-making or re-grant of the Pastoral Lease from time to time;

• the grant of licence, permit, or authorisation from time to time, including any amendment or renewal, re-making or re-granting of the Pastoral Lease, to conduct activities for agricultural purposes (including the diversification and intensification of pastoral related activities) on the Pastoral Lease;

• the grant of leases, licences and permits from time to time to conduct low impact tourism activity in the Pastoral Lease; and

• the grant of a pastoral lease from time to time in relation to all or part of any Stock Route or Reserve, to the extent and in the terms of schedule 2 of the agreement.

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The agreement is located within the area of native title recognised by the Federal Court of Australia (FCA) in the proceeding Lyndon on behalf of the Budina People v State of Western Australia [2017] FCA 1214 (Budina People) (FCA File No.: WAD131/2004; NNTT File No.: WCD2017/006)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2017/020"^^xsd:anyURI .

