idn-resource:36e370e0-4c8e-5d65-89d2-91f43570ed02 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:7b928a0d-47c5-537a-9136-066ae7f542f4 ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A003914"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "3914"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Wintinna Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between the State of South Australia (APPLICANT) and Jean Wood, Sadie Singer, Lallie Lennon, Johnny Cullinan on behalf of the Yankunytjatjara Antakirinja; and Bakiss Pty Ltd, Digby Giles & Bernadette Elizabeth Giles. The ILUA was registered on 18 June 2007.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide access for the Yankunytjatjara/Antakirinja people to conduct traditional activities over the ILUA area."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:9e5e8f61-69be-5e2a-a9cd-58fb000349bd,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=3914> ;
    schema:name "The Wintinna Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2007-06-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """This ILUA does not include any statements regarding 'future acts', nor does it alter the right to negotiate over future acts, as set out in the relevant Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) provisions. Under this Act any activity, such as a grant of land, that may affect native title rights is defined as a 'future act' and must comply with the future act provisions of the Act in order to be valid.

This ILUA is one of several that has resulted from the De Rose Hill native title determination (De Rose v State of South Australia (No 2) [2005] FCAFC 110) of the Yankunytjatjara/Antakirinja native title claim."""@en .

idn-resource:36e5c146-b5a1-5942-864c-7c6fb48ae30f a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:7b928a0d-47c5-537a-9136-066ae7f542f4 ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A004264"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "4264"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Eastern Kuku Yalanji, the State of Queensland & Cook Shire Council Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between Agnes Walker, Eileen Walker, Hazel Douglas, John Walker Jnr and Peter Fischer (Native Title Parties); the State of Queensland; and the Cook Shire Council on 19 October 2007.

The purpose of this ILUA is for the creation of reserves and roads under the Land Act 1994 (Qld) within the agreement area. The ILUA also provides for the manner of exercise of native title rights and interests within the agreement area.

This ILUA includes agreement that 'future acts' may be done. The parties also agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to future acts, as the alternative consultation provisions are to be followed instead. Under this Act any activity, such as a grant of land, that may affect native title rights is defined as a ‘future act’ and must comply with the future act provisions of the Act in order to be valid."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:5996de0c-8cc6-5f14-8901-d839af36a4d4,
        atns-sub:7cc37d9a-fe3c-5fec-b115-d1bb8d72db9c,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:b9cb4d2e-5a5b-57ae-a2ac-5450c37a61d8,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=4264> ;
    schema:name "Eastern Kuku Yalanji, the State of Queensland & Cook Shire Council Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2007-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The Eastern Kuku Yalanji people, the State of Queensland and the Cook Shire Council will co-manage a reserve. This agreement sees the Rossville tip, the Rossville Community hall and Rossville Sport and a recreation facility designated as a reserve under the Land Act 1994 (Qld).

This ILUA is one of 15 resulting from the Eastern Kuku Yalanji 1994 native title claim over some 144,000 hectares, which was mainly timber reserve and unallocated Crown land. In 1997 the Eastern Kuku Yalanji proposed a settlement with the Queensland Government, which was agreed to in principle by most parties in 2005 (Queensland Government). Approximately 250,000 hectares of land were given back to the Eastern Kuku Yalanji people with 64,000 hectares designated as freehold land to be used for conservation with 16,500 of this proportion to be set aside for use as residential or economic development. The majority of the land will be co-managed by the Eastern Kuku Yalanji people and the Queensland Parks & Wildlife Service (QPWS) (The Australian). At the sign-off in Wujal Wujal in April 2007, then premier Peter Beattie congratulated all involved in the process, saying that it was ‘the most significant ILUA [sic] ever struck in Queensland’ (Kantri Leif)."""@en .

idn-resource:36e6e122-82c0-5998-88fc-3930b02770ce a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
