    schema:description """Arrow Darumbal LNG Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) No.2 is an Area Agreement between:

- Arrow Energy Pty Ltd; and

- Alan Douglas Hatfield, Warren John Malone, Rodney William Mann, Vanessa Ross, Amanda Meredith and Pauline Cora as the Registered Native Title Claimant for Native Title Determination Application QUD6131/1998 on their own behalf and on behalf of the Darumbal People.

The purpose of this Agreement is to provide consent for the exploration, extraction, collection, processing or production of, natural gas within the ILUA Area."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:35e19906-2659-5157-8aee-b9d82eedbb1c,
        atns-sub:81edd075-cb8e-5a7e-a65d-a47cec815898,
        atns-sub:97be12ad-fd1c-5136-9323-0929eb90b556,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6917> ;
    schema:name "Arrow Darumbal LNG Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) No.2"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2015-018> ;
    schema:startDate "2015-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement

The Agreement commences on the Execution Date, being 2 June 2015. The Extract does not specify the end date for the Agreement.

The Right to Negotiate

The Agreement states that Part 2 Division 3 Subdivision P of the Native Title Act (in respect of the right to negotiate) does not apply to any Agreed Project Activities covered by the Agreement.

Project Activities

Clause 11.1 of the Agreement states that the Parties consent to the Project Activities, including:

Exploration and Production Related Activities
(a) the exploration, extraction, collection, processing or production of, natural gas;
(b) the extraction, collection, processing, production or use of water derived from the process of extracting natural gas;
(c) agricultural activities which use water of the kind referred to in paragraph (b);
(d) anything permitting or requiring any of the things referred to paragraphs (a), (b) and (c).

Gas Transmission Related Activities
(a) the collection, distribution, transmission or transportation of natural gas;
(b) the collection, distribution, transmission or transportation of water derived from the process of extracting natural gas;
(c) any Looping Project;
(d) anything permitting or requiring any of the things referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c).

Schedule 4 of the Agreement sets out some examples of acts which constitute or may constitute Agreed Project Activities (see the link below). Examples include:
- grant, variation, extension, renewal or re-grant of a lease
- grant, variation, extension, renewal or re-grant of an easement
- grant, variation, extension, renewal or re-grant of a pipeline license
- dedication, opening of and changes to a road

Native Title in the Agreement Area

The Agreement area falls within two native title applications by the Darumbal People (QUD6131/1998 and QUD6131/1998)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2015/018"^^xsd:anyURI .

