idn-resource:428c9982-f771-5d0b-9802-cdbb3f99e45c a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007177"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7177"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:123a2199-09c1-53e0-9c4d-6ae2033ea91c ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Overarching Bilateral Indigenous Plan (OBIP) provides a platform for implementing the partnership under the National Indigenous Reform Agreement in South Australia.

It establishes how the Parties will work together with Indigenous communities to realise the COAG commitments and objectives of 'Closing the Gap', within the specific context of South Australia."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:d15dd1de-4696-50c8-9f10-2e95eea88e6f,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7177> ;
    schema:name "Overarching Bilateral Plan between the Commonwealth of Australia and the State of South Australia to Close the Gap in Indigenous Disadvantage 2010-2015"@en ;
    schema:text """The plan sets out the agreed positions on principles underpinning bilateral plans; priority areas for bilateral action; arrangements for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander representation and consultation with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people across South Australia; and Whole of government machinery.

Context

The Plan sets out the applicable policy frameworks and agreements, including ‘Closing the Gap’ COAG agreements. It also sets out the demographic context in South Australia, providing a data snapshot of the Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander population.

Arrangements for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander consultation and representation

The Governments will work with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people to determine arrangements for consultation and representation. Engagement and partnership will be guided by a range of mechanisms through which governments partnerships, include jurisdictional advisory groups, and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander expert organisations
National Congress of Australia’s First Peoples will be the peak body for advice on the implementation of OBIPs

Joint machinery

The Parties will ensure effective implementation and evaluation of measurable outcomes under this Plan via joint Ministerial oversight and reporting; an OBIP Working Group to review and jointly report on progress of reforms and other activities; establishing or strengthening joint coordination arrangements, including those outlined in National Partnership Agreements; and where possible aligning Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander reporting obligations.

The Terms of Reference for the South Australian Overarching Bilateral Indigenous Plan Working Group are at Clause 34 of the Plan."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.papertracker.com.au/pdfs/bilateral_plan_2010_2015.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:4291472e-e618-5550-844e-5930d754cde2 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007795"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7795"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Nyiyaparli and BHP Billiton Comprehensive Agreement Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between:

• BHP Billiton Iron Ore Pty Ltd for and on behalf of BHP Billiton Minerals Pty Ltd as agent, BHP Iron Ore (Jimblebar) Pty Ltd) as agent, BHP Direct Reduced Iron Pty Ltd as agent, the participants in the Mount Goldsworthy Mining Associates Joint Venture as at the commencement date as manager and agent, the participants in the Mt Newman Mining Associates Joint Venture as at the commencement date as manager and agent, and the participants in the Yandi Joint Venture as at the commencement sate as manager and agent; and

• the Karika Nyiyaparli Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body corporate (RNTBC).

The purpose of the agreement is for the native title holders to consent to BHP Billiton's Iron Ore Business.

The Native Title Representative Bodies for the ILUA area is Central Desert Native Title Services and the Yamatji Marlpa Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7795> ;
    schema:name "Nyiyaparli and BHP Billiton Comprehensive Agreement Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2019-003> ;
    schema:startDate "2019-07-01"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

Commencement:

The ILUA commences on the date signed by all parties, 1 July 2019. It operates as an ILUA from the date of its registration, 6 September 2019.

Termination:

The ILUA will terminate on the earlier of:

• the termination of the Comprehensive Agreement between the Nyiyaparli People and BHP Billiton, as amended from time to time;

• the written agreement of the parties; or

• if removed from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) are not intended to apply to the agreed future acts.

Extinguishment

Future act provisions

The parties consent to BHP Billiton's Iron Ore Business, meaning the elements of iron ore exploration, mining, transport, processing, and treatment in the Pilbara region, and all acts incidental to it including the granting of all interests or approvals necessary.

The Karlka Nyiyaparli Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC and the Nyiyaparli People agree to do all lawful things within their power to assist in the granting of the approvals and all elements of BHP Billiton's Iron Ore Business, as well as to not encourage or assist any other person to challenge the validity of BHP Billiton's Irone Ore Business.

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The ILUA area is within the area of the native title determination Stock on behalf of the Nyiaparli People v State of Western Australia (No 5) [2018] FCA 1453."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2019/003"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:4292e1c9-1d42-5a2f-9a67-379ea05ba79e a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A003036"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "3412"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:51e799aa-68a2-5df5-b3b6-ce3837c24612 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Co-operation – Land Council Intra-Aboriginal Agreement is a template Intra-Aboriginal Agreement provided by the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT).

It is envisaged by the NNTT that these agreements will be used to assist parties to negotiate Intra-Aboriginal Agreements that can be tailored to their specific needs and circumstances.

The Co-operation – Land Council Agreement is designed to be used for negotiations between native title claimants and a Native Title Representative Body. It is envisaged that this Agreement would be used where disputes had arisen between both people within the native title party, and between the native title party and the Land Council that represents them.

The template agreement covers matters including the setting up of an Independent Body made up of members of the native title party, funded by the Land Council. This Independent Body would represent the Aboriginal group asserting native title over the particular area. Once set up, the Independent Body would invite expressions of interest for their native title legal representation, as well as being responsible for negotiating with mining companies."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:61167f4a-3766-5848-9d7f-369aa9ebd427,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=3412> ;
    schema:name "Co-operation - Land Council Intra-Aboriginal  Agreement"@en ;
    schema:text """The NNTT has issued template agreements covering six categories, being:
1. Future Act Agreements
2. Intra-Aboriginal Agreements
3. Mediation Withdrawal Agreements
4. Negotiating Framework Agreements
5. Pastoral Agreements
6. Reconciliation Agreements Principals.

Please see the ‘Template Agreement’ link at the bottom of this page for further information.

Please see the National Native Title Tribunal's DISCLAIMER in relation to these agreements."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/agreements/files/TemplateCoOpLandCouncilIAA/"^^xsd:anyURI .

