idn-resource:48323405-713d-58d2-9d1d-fdf7debe09d1 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A005922"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "5922"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Combined Mandingalbay Yidinji Gunggandji Yarrabah DOGIT Transfer Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is an agreement between:

- the State of Queensland (applicant);
- Les Murgha and Charles Garling on their own behalf and on behalf of the Gunggandji People;
- Vincent Mundraby on his own behalf and on behalf of the Mandingalbay Yidinji People; and
- the Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council.

The agreement was made on 12/09/2011.

The purpose of this agreement is for the parties to provide their consent to the transfer of an area of land under the Aboriginal Land Act 1991 (Qld) (ALA) and the granting of that land as Aboriginal Land."""@en ;
    schema:endDate "2014-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:4f924c21-9e16-51f1-823e-8944b84c7142,
        atns-sub:710c226b-1fba-5eba-86c9-5087f506ac80,
        atns-sub:746b3b59-88ea-5685-81f7-1558875d7c47,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5922> ;
    schema:name "Combined Mandingalbay Yidinji Gunggandji Yarrabah DOGIT Transfer Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2011-09-12"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

Commencement

Most of the ILUA provisions commence on the date of execution, 12 September 2011, but Clause 5 of the ILUA commences on the termination of the Yarrabah Blockholders ILUA [Tribunal file number QI2011/054].

The Agreement terminates on 1 January 2014, subject to a deed for the Aboriginal Land Act 1991 (Qld)(ALA) Transfer Area being delivered.

Native Title parties' consent

The parties to this agreement consent to the ALA Transfer Area being granted as Aboriginal Land.

The Native Title parties agree that they will not object to the granting of the ALA Transfer Area as Aboriginal Land, or do anything that prevents or delays the granting of Aboriginal Land.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Federal Court determination Mundraby & Ors on behalf of the Combined Mandingalbay Yidinji - Gunggandji Claim v State of Queensland (unreported, FCA, 21 September 2012, Dowsett J) recognised that native title exists over approximately 82 square kilometres of the Combined Mandingalbay Yidinji-Gunggandji People’s traditional land."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/QLD_-_Registered_ILUA_-_Combined_Mandingalbay_Yidinji_Gunggandji_Yarrabah_DOGIT_Transfer_ILUA_QI2011_55.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

