    schema:description """Project: Rio Tinto Exploration
Summary: The Far West Coast (SA) Agreement represents an historic process of negotiation between 14 Mining companies and five Aboriginal groups providing access for exploration to the Far West Region. It is a model agreement based on common sense and a willingness of Aboriginal groups to work with the mining industry. Aboriginal clearance work was funded by the exploration companies."""@en ;
