    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Newcrest Mining Project Area Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between the Western Desert Lands Aboriginal Corporation and Newcrest Operations Limited on 4 December 2015. The ILUA is to set up a body corporate for the agreement."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7292> ;
    schema:name "Newcrest Mining Project Area Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2015-022> ;
    schema:startDate "2015-12-04"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement: The ILUA is located in the Shire of East Pilbara. It is located covers about 11,150 sq km, approx. 60km radius from Telfer Mine Site and generally north-west along Telfer Access Road towards Gregory Range.

Commencement The ILUA commenced on 4 December 2015.

Native Title Provisions
The ILUA does have statements that reference subsection 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth).

Background to the Agreement: The ILUA allows access to the land for infrastructure and mining.

Native Title in the ILUA Area
The land which the ILUA is subject to is part of the Marta Determination Area. The 'Martu Determination Area' means the land and waters over which the Martu People were determined to hold native title rights and interests in the Martu Determinations."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2015/022"^^xsd:anyURI .

