    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Tjayiwara Unmuru – Ayers Range South Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between:

- The Attorney-General for the State of South Australia;

- Peter De Rose and Mary Anderson for and on behalf of the Tjayiwara Unmuru People;

- Tjayiwara Unmuru Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC;

- Colin Bruce Morton; and

- Lyndavale Pty Ltd

on 25 March 2014.

The purpose of this Body Corporate Agreement is to provide consent for access to the Agreement Area, conduct of traditional activities and consultation related to heritage protection."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6378> ;
    schema:name "Tjayiwara Unmuru – Ayers Range South Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2014-03-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement

This ILUA was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT) on 25 March 2014.

The Extract does not note specific start or end dates for this Body Corporate Agreement.

The Extract does state, however, that the Agreement commences on the Date of Registration, being 25 March 2014. The Agreement operates for an indefinite term.

Native Title Provisions

The Agreement does not contain any statements of a kind mentioned in either s24EB(1) or s24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act.

The Extract does not provide considerable information regarding the impact of the Agreement. The most illuminating statement within the Extract states that the Agreement concerns the interrelationship between "native title rights and interests and other rights and interests in relation to the agreement area, and generally relates to access, the conduct of traditional activities and consultation related to heritage protection."

Native Title in the ILUA Area.

The Area includes all land and waters subject to Pastoral Lease Number 2491, known as
Ayers Range South. This area does not include any existing public roads. The area falls within Native Title Determination application SAD208/2010 Tjayiwara Unmuru Native Title Claim (SC2010/5), accepted for registration on 5 October 2011."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/SA_-_Registered_ILUA_-_Tjayiwara_Unmuru_–_Ayers_Range_South_Pastoral_ILUA_SI2014_002.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

