    schema:description """The Allandale Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between the State of South Australia (APPLICANT); Jean Wood, Sadie Singer, Lallie Lennon, Johnny Cullinan; and Andrew Trevor Clarke on 4 June 2007.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide access for the Yankunytjatjara/Antakirinja people to conduct traditional activities on the crown lease known as Allandale.

The ILUA extract does not stipulate how long the agreement will run for."""@en ;
