idn-resource:637610b5-eed7-5bd0-ad21-c2a76e3911d1 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007696"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7696"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The PKKP and Nanutarra Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between Red Sky Stations Pty Ltd and PKKP Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate (RNTBC).

The Agreement Area covers about 681 sq km, located about 199 sq km approximately 190 km west of Tom Price.

The purpose of the Agreement is to consent to access, pastoral activities and low impact tourism.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Yamatji Marlpa Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:f630e08a-ea9c-57e3-ab87-066e4b9ad57e,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7696> ;
    schema:name "PKKP and Nanutarra Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2016-009> ;
    schema:startDate "2017-01-04"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

Commencement:

The Agreement commences in full on the date of registration, 4 January 2017.

Termination:

The Agreement, except for the Clause 21 and obligations accured before termination, terminates automatically upon the end of the Pastoral Lease or by written agreement of all the Parties.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate:

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth)will not apply with respect to the agreed future acts in the Agreement.

Future Act Provisions:

The Extract notes that there are statements within the Agreement of the kind which are mentioned in ss 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), and so the consequences set out under those sections are triggered by this agreement. This means that the Agreement provides consent for the doing of certain acts by non-native title parties. Specifically this Agreement provides consent for the doing of the following future acts:

• the renewal, re-making or re-grant of the Pastoral Lease from time to time;

• the grant of licence, permit, or authorisation from time to time, including any amendment or renewal, re-making or re-granting of the Pastoral Lease, to conduct activities for agricultural purposes (including the diversification and intensification of pastoral related activities) on the Pastoral Lease;

• the grant of leases, licences and permits from time to time to conduct Low Impact Tourism activity in the Pastoral Lease; and

• the grant of pastoral lease from time to time in relation to all or part of any Stock Route or Reserve, to the extent and in the terms of clause 12 of this ILUA.

Native Title in the Area:

The ILUA is located within the area of native title recognised in the Federal Court of Australia (FCA) proceeding Puutu Kunti Kurrama and Pinikura 2 (FCA File No.: WAD126/2005; NNTT File No.: WC2005/004)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2016/009"^^xsd:anyURI .

