    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Hughenden Industrial Estate Indigenous Land Use Agreement was made between the State of Queensland, Flinders Shire Council and the Yirandali native title group of north Queensland. Under the agreement approximately 35 hectares of land is transferred into freehold for the Hughenden Industrial Estate, and 2 hectares is transferred into freehold for use by the Yirandali traditional owners.

Freehold title is granted to the State over the Hughenden Pasturage Reserve Freehold; and Gravel Reserve Freehold is granted to the Council.

Native title rights and interests in the area of the ILUA have been surrendered - the effect of this is that any native title rights and interests that may have existed in the area are extinguished."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
