    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:caa3eeb7-4d71-505c-9ee9-19b8c5338435 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """Between: Robert Anderson and Evelyn Parkin on behalf of the Quandamooka People (Mulgumpin/Moreton Island Claim) (Applicant)

And

State of Queensland, Commonwealth of Australia and Brisbane City Council (Respondents)

Judge: Justice Rangiah

Where made: [ONLY INSERT PLACE NAME IF MADE ON COUNTRY/ OTHERWISE DELETE THIS HEADING]

Determination

Native title exists in [INSERT in the entire/ OR parts] of the determination area

It consists of exclusive and non-exclusive native title rights and interests, in relation to the areas described in Parts 1 and 2 of Schedule 2. fill in other parts- complicated & need to re-read

Native title holders

Native title is held by the Quandamooka People, as described in Schedule One.

Exclusive native title rights and interests over [INSERT all/or part] of the determination area

This is the right to possession, occupation, use, and enjoyment of the area, described in Part 1 of Schedule 2 other than in relation to water, to the exclusion of all others.

Non-exclusive native title rights and interests over [INSERT all/ or part] of the determination area

These rights exist over the area described in Part 2 of Schedule 2 and include rights to:

• live and be present on the area;

• take, use, share and exchange natural resources of the area for personal, domestic and non-commercial communal purposes;

• conduct burial rites;

• conduct ceremonies;

• teach on the area about its physical and spiritual attributes;

• maintain and protect important places on Country;

• light fires for domestic purposes, except hunting or clearing vegetation;

• be accompanied by

Other rights and interests in the determination area include:

• [bullet point list]

See Schedule [INSERT SCHEDULE NAME/NUMBER] for further information about the non-native title rights and interests. [IF THIS SENTENCE IS NOT APPLICABLE DELETE IT]

In the case of conflict, the exercise of non-native title rights and interests will prevail over the non-exclusive native title

The [INSERT NAME] Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate (RNTBC) is the prescribed body corporate. It performs the functions required under the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) and [INSERT acts as agent / OR holds the native title in trust] for the [INSERT THE NAME OF THE NATIVE TITLE HOLDERS].

Full text of the determination is available via the URL link above."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=8256> ;
    schema:name "Anderson on behalf of Quandamooka People (Mulgumpin/Moreton Island Claim) v State of Queensland (No.2) [2019] FCA 2001 IN PROGRESS"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2020-05-29"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Background

[INSERT progression of the claim and any media references]

Details of Judgment

