    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Northern NSW Integrated Aboriginal Health and Wellbeing Plan 2015-2020 Partnership Agreement ('the Agreement') seeks to commit parties to working collaboratively on the Northern NSW Integrated Aboriginal Health and Wellbeing Plan 2015-2020 ('the Plan') and achieving its vision.

Signatories:
Northern NSW Local Health District (NNSW LHD)
North Coast Primary Health Network
Northern NSW Bullinah Aboriginal Health Service
Bulgarr Ngaru Medical Aboriginal Corporation
NSW Police – Northern Region
NSW Department of Education and Communities
Aboriginal Learning Circle – North Coast Institute of Technical and Further education
NSW Family and Community Services – Northern District"""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:d15dd1de-4696-50c8-9f10-2e95eea88e6f,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7193> ;
    schema:name "Northern New South Wales Integrated Aboriginal Health and Wellbeing Plan 2015-2020 Partnership Agreement"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2015-08-03"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commitments under the Agreement include:
- Each party agrees to implement the Plan and report on progress through their respective established reporting practices;
- The Plan will be rolled out over 5 years;
- The Manager NNSW LHD Aboriginal Health will host yearly meetings of all parties to report on progress against the Plan; and
- The Northern NSW Aboriginal Health Partnership and NNSW LHD Health Services Development Committee will oversee progress against the Plan and its evaluation."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://nnswlhd.health.nsw.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/1508043-NNSW-Integrated-Aboriginal-Health-Wellbeing-Plan-Partnership-Agreement.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

