    schema:description """Between: Payi Payi & Ors On Behalf Of The Ngururrpa People (APPLICANTS)

AND

The State of Western Australia (RESPONDENTS)

Judge: Black CJ
Where: Yakka Yakka Road, South of Balgo, Western Australia
Determination: Native Title exists over the entire determination area.

Other matters that were determined include that the native title holders have a year from the date of this determination to nominate a Prescribed Body Corporate, and that a small overlap with the Tjurabalan determination resulted with a small portion of this application being dismissed."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=4199> ;
    schema:name "Payi Payi on behalf of the Ngururrpa people v the State of Western Australia (Unreported, FCA, 18 October 2007, Black CJ)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2007-10-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """On 8 December 2006, the Ngurpurra people lodged native title claim WAD357/06 with the Federal Court. The matter was referred for mediation on 14 June 2007, and on 18 October 2007 representatives of the State of Western Australia and the Ngururrpa people reached agreement that native title should be recognised over approximately 30,000 square kilometres in the Great Sandy Desert of Western Australia.

The determination has been lauded for its constructive negotiation process and quick resolution by tribunal member Ruth Wade.

The determination recognises exclusive native title rights to possess, occupy, use and enjoy the area of the determination. One exception to this is the flowing and subterranean waters, where the native title holders have the non-exclusive right to take water for personal, domestic or non-commercial purposes. These non-exclusive rights include the right to take and use ochre."""@en .

