    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The NSW Aboriginal Health Partnership Agreement 2015-2025 ('the Agreement') recognises the ongoing partnership between the NSW Government health portfolio and the peak body for community-controlled health services in New South Wales in the joint endeavour to improve health and well being outcomes for Aboriginal people in NSW.

Signatories:
- NSW Ministry of Health
- Aboriginal Health and Medical Research Council of New South Wales"""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:d15dd1de-4696-50c8-9f10-2e95eea88e6f,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7180> ;
    schema:name "New South Wales Aboriginal Health Partnership Agreement 2015-2025"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2015-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The Agreement reaffirms the 20-year-strong partnership, and recognises that community-controlled health services promote the right to self-determination and delivers culturally appropriate primary health care for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. The partnership responsibilities include ensuring that Aboriginal health remains a priority for Closing the Gap; and is an integral part of NSW Health services.

Partnership meetings are to be scheduled as agreed and will be co-chaired by both parties, and have agendas jointly determined."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.health.nsw.gov.au/aboriginal/Documents/Aboriginal-Health-Partnership-Agreement.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

