    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Illmargani Conservation Agreement was entered into in April 2000, between The State of Queensland and the Cowley Family, the owners of a sheep and cattle property ‘North Yancho’ in southwest Queensland. The Agreement is in relation to land on North Yancho which had been declared a Nature Reserve and listed on the State Register. The Agreement has been registered on the title of North Yancho. One of the conditions of the Conservation Agreement is that the Gunggari people have access to the area in recognition of their traditional ownership of the land."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
