    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Town of Tennant Creek Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between the Central Land Council (APPLICANT), the Northern Territory of Australia and the Patta Aboriginal Corporation on 22 February 2008. The purpose of the ILUA is to provide statements pursuant to the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) (NTA) which, in relation to the 'Surrender Area', detail the past extinguishment of native title, the surrender and extinguishment of native title by the Patta Aboriginal Corporation on behalf of the native title holders and also that the right to negotiate under the NTA does not apply to this agreement.

The ILUA was registered on 22 February 2008, and does not have a stipulated period of operation."""@en ;
