idn-resource:8116d439-1000-52a8-8771-c548965629e3 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006912"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6912"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """Garawa People Wentworth Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is an Area Agreement between:

- Terrance Taylor and Jacky Green on their own behalf and on behalf of the Gangalidda and Garawa People (applicant);

- Gangalidda and Garawa Native Title Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC as agent for and on behalf of the Garawa People; and

- Panoy Pty Ltd.

The purpose of this Agreement is to set out the terms of access to the Agreement Area, over which the Garawa People will gain access to and exercise the Native Title Rights and Interests."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6912> ;
    schema:name "Garawa People Wentworth Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2015-010> ;
    schema:startDate "2015-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement

The Agreement commences on the Commencement date, specified by the Agreement Extract as 26 March 2015.

Cessation

Subject to clause 8.4, the Agreement is to continue until:
(a) the date of expiry of the Lease term; or
(b) the date of surrender, resumption, forfeiture or termination of the Lease; or
(c) the date of removal of the Agreement from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements.

Clause 8.4 of the Agreement states that unless otherwise agreed, this Agreement will end with the valid extinguishment of Native Title over the whole of the Agreement Area.

Native Title in the Agreement Area

The Agreement area falls within the Garawa People native title determination.

By consent, a determination was made on 23 June 2010 (QC04/05 and QC95/03; Gangalidda and Garawa People v State of Queensland [2010] FCA 646) recognising the Gangalidda and Garawa Peoples' native title rights over 5,810 sq km of land and waters, including exclusive native title rights over an Aboriginal Land Trust area and Aboriginal owned pastoral leases."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2015/010"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:81226c79-61ad-5c8a-acc3-7d24503be3f3 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006089"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6089"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The SCONI Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is an agreement between:
- Metallica Minerals Limited;
- NORNICO Pty Ltd;
- Ernest Hoolihan, Harry Gertz, Narda Kennedy, Hazel Illin and Elsie Thompson on their own behalf and for and on behalf of all Gugu Badhun People;
- Ms Beryl Buller; and
- Gugu Badhun Aboriginal Corporation.

The purpose of the agreement is for the parties to give their authorisation and consent to agreed Future Acts."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:35e19906-2659-5157-8aee-b9d82eedbb1c,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6089> ;
    schema:name "SCONI Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2012-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

Commencement

The agreement commences on the date of registration with the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT), which is 18 December 2012, and will terminate upon occurrence of the earlier of the following:
(a) on the date that Metallica Group ceases to hold any right, title or interest in relation to any of the Projects in the Agreement Area and the giving by Metallica Group of 20 Business Day's written notice to the Native Title Party to this effect;
(b) on the date of the making of a Contrary Determination and the giving by Metallica Group of 20 Business Day's written notice to the Native Title Party to this effect; or
(c) the parties agreeing in writing to terminate this Agreement.

Parties consent

For the purposes of section 24EB(1)(c) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth)('NTA'), the Parties acknowledge and agree that the right to negotiate provision contained in Subdivision P of Division 3 of Part 2 of the NTA is not intended to apply and does not apply to the Future Agreed Acts.

The Parties consent to Future Agreed Acts as of and from the commencement date (18 December 2012).

“Future Agreed Acts” means;
(a) The Grant of the Future Titles;
(b) The conduct of the Activities or the Grant of any act, including additional related or associated acts that are reasonably required to give effect to the Future Titles; and
(c) The construction, operation, use maintenance and repair of all plant and infrastructure required for the Projects including, but not limited to, roads, pipeline and power lines, within the Agreement Area.

“Future titles” means any Exploration Permit for Minerals, Mineral Development Licence, Mining Leases or other approval, permit or licence (including infrastructure approvals,environmental approvals and water approvals) within the Agreement Area which is required for the Projects and applied for by Metallica Group.

“Metallica Group” means:
(a) Metallica Minerals;
(b) NORNICO;
(c) any Related Body Corporate of either Metallica Minerals or NORNICO which is involved in any way with any one or more of the Projects and who has executed a deed of covenant in a form reasonably satisfactory to the Parties; and
(d) any other person who is involved in a Joint Venture with any of the above entities, in respect of one or more of the Projects, where the Joint Venture identifies one of the above entities of this definition as the Manager of the Joint Venture.

Native Title in the ILUA area

In the consent determination of Gugu Badhun People #2, the Federal Court of Australia recognised the native title rights and interests of the Gugu Badhum People to an area of about 6,540 sq kms, located approximately 40 kms west of Ingham in Queensland. The consent determination was handed down in a Federal Court hearing on 1 August 2012 by Justice John Logan. The determination recognises the Gugu Badhun People’s exclusive and non-exclusive native title rights."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/QLD_-_Registered_ILUA_-_SCONI_Project_ILUA_QI2012_069.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:8126afcd-c68e-5ecc-a8e4-5687ff4414f7 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A005592"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "5592"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Yarrabah Blockholders Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is an area agreement made between the State of Queensland (Applicant), Les Murgha on his own behalf and on behalf of the Gunggandji People and the Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council. The agreement commences on 19 April 2011 and terminates on 4 October 2013. The purpose of the ILUA is to allow for the granting of leases by the Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council over the agreement area."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:4f924c21-9e16-51f1-823e-8944b84c7142,
        atns-sub:710c226b-1fba-5eba-86c9-5087f506ac80,
        atns-sub:7cc37d9a-fe3c-5fec-b115-d1bb8d72db9c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5592> ;
    schema:name "Yarrabah Blockholders Indigenous Land Use Agreement"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2011-10-04"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Terms of the Agreement
The parties to the Yarrabah Blockholders ILUA consent to the trustee of the deed of grant in trust (DOGIT), being the Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council, granting a lease within the agreement area to a defined person known as a blockholder. The Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council may grant a lease to a blockholder for purposes, and over areas, specified in the ILUA if the Gunggandji People, the Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council, the State of Queensland and the particular blockholder execute an Opt in Deed.

The ILUA also allows for the Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council to grant a lease over land within the agreement area if there has been consent or deemed consent by the Gungandji People under the ILUA.

Any lease granted under the agreement is to be granted under the Aboriginal Land Act 1991 (Qld) for a term for 30 years.

Background
Native title history
Mr Les Murgha and Mr Stewart Harris, on behalf of the Combined Gunggandji People are currently seeking a determination of native title pursuant to the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth). The claim area lies to the south of Cairns, borders Mission Bay and includes the Yarrabah township. There are numerous respondents including the State of Queensland, Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council, Ergon Energy Corporation Limited, Telstra Corporation Limited, numerous fisherman and others. The application was accepted for registration in 2008 having passed the registration test."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/QLD_-_Registered_ILUA_-_Yarrabah_Blockholders_ILUA_QI2011_013.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

