    schema:description "RTA Weipa Pty Ltd and Ngan Aak-Kunch Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between RTA Weipa Pty Ltd and Ngan Aak-Kunch Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC on 21 April 2016. The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for a range of acts, whether or not they are 'future acts' regarding the access to a body corporate agreement. The agreement area is within the external boundary of the claim area for the Wik and Wik Way People."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7346> ;
    schema:name "RTA Weipa Pty Ltd and Ngan Aak-Kunch Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2016-002> ;
    schema:startDate "2016-04-21"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement: The ILUA is located in the Aurukun Shire Council. The Agreement Area is located approximately 38 km northeast of Aurukun. The Area consists of a 27km long, generally 4 metre wide corridor and covers approximately 0.11 sq km.

Commencement: The ILUA commenced on 21 April 2016.

Native Title Provisions: The ILUA does have statements that reference subsection 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth).

Background to the Agreement: The ILUA is primarily in relation to access to the land for the body corporate.

Native Title in the ILUA Area: The ILUA is in the native title claim area which includes the land and waters subject to the Federal Court determination Wik and Wik Way Native Title Claim Group v State of Queensland (QUD6029/2001)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2016/002"^^xsd:anyURI .

