    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A002545"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "2945"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336,
        atns-subcat:cb04592a-0221-592e-9bd2-7cfd7c515db8 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Native Title Petroleum Agreement between the Northern Land Council and Pardi Pty Ltd (the Agreement) was signed in 2003. It paves the way for the valid grant of a petroleum exploration licence by the Northern Territory Government with the consent of the traditional owners."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:17d993e0-d19e-5349-a48e-4de57b1dba59,
        atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:35e19906-2659-5157-8aee-b9d82eedbb1c,
        atns-sub:6a8815da-e29d-506f-85fd-c64c8807fea2,
        atns-sub:97be12ad-fd1c-5136-9323-0929eb90b556,
        atns-sub:9e5e8f61-69be-5e2a-a9cd-58fb000349bd,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:e52a2091-dcda-569c-aafb-6497428c615c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Newcastle Waters region, Northern Territory, Australia"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=2945> ;
    schema:name "Native Title Petroleum Agreement between the Northern Land Council and Pardi Pty Ltd"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2003-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The Agreement is one of the first of its kind to be mediated in the Northern Territory and establishes the terms of exploration and production as well as protections for sacred sites and the environment. A similar agreement has been negotiated with Sweetpea Corporation by the NLC on behalf of the traditional owners over land adjacent to the Pardi site.

It is envisaged that the agreements, made under the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) will function as templates for further petroleum exploration agreements relating to the sedimentary basins of the Northern Territory. In addition, the agreements are to provide employment and training opportunities for local Aboriginal people where any discoveries are commercialised."""@en .

idn-resource:91779a97-2db0-5baf-b1a4-93452f8fe5de a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A004719"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "4719"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The 'Central Petroleum and others and Central Land Council Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) re Exploration' was concluded between the Central Land Council (APPLICANT)and Central Petroleum Ltd, Helium Australia Pty Ltd, Ordiv Petroleum Pty Ltd and Frontier Oil & Gas Pty Ltd. The agreement was registered on 13 June 2008.

The purpose of the ILUA is to grant exploration permits in the proposed areas and set the terms under which Central Petroleum and its subsidiary companies agree to exercise their rights under the permits."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:35e19906-2659-5157-8aee-b9d82eedbb1c,
        atns-sub:5996de0c-8cc6-5f14-8901-d839af36a4d4,
        atns-sub:81edd075-cb8e-5a7e-a65d-a47cec815898,
        atns-sub:97be12ad-fd1c-5136-9323-0929eb90b556,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=4719> ;
    schema:name "Central Petroleum and others and Central Land Council Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)re: Exploration Permits 82, 112, 118 and 125"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2008-06-13"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The ILUA covers all matters relating to the grant and use of the permits and the terms and conditions applicable for any future Production Agreements in the permit area.

To the extent that the grant of the permits is a future act as defined in the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), the Land Council consents to exploration subject to the terms and conditions of the ILUA. The right to negotiate under the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) was excluded by the ILUA."""@en .

