idn-resource:91f4899a-acb4-56ee-a9b3-c0692f0eddbe a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007597"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7597"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Waanyi - Burke Shire Council (Gregory Solar Farm Project) Indigenous Land Agreement ('ILUA') was agreed under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) between:

• the Waanyi Native Title Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate (RNTBC),

• the Burke Shire Council, and

• the State of Queensland acting through the Department of Natural Resources and Mines Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Land Services.

The purpose of the agreement is to provide consent for the surrender of the Waanyi People's native title rights and interests over the two lots within the agreement area.

The agreement area covers about 14 ha, consisting of Lot 11 on AP13658 and part of Lot 5 on SP265803 within the township of Gregory, in the vicinity of the Gregory Showground. The area is about 105 km south of Burketown.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Carpentaria Land Council Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:dbff1607-a2a3-5baf-995d-8c9bb0552665,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7597> ;
    schema:name "Waanyi - Burke Shire Council (Gregory Solar Farm Project) Indigenous Land Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2017-003> ;
    schema:startDate "2017-03-12"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The agreement area consists all the land and waters of Lot 11 on AP13658 and the part of Lot 5 on SP265803.

Commencement:

The agreement commenced on 12 March 2017 (the date that the last party signed the agreement). The surrender of native title (clause 7 of the agreement) commences on 22 June 2017 (the registration date).

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to the surrender of the Waanyi Peopls's native title rights and interests as consented to under this agreement.

Extinguishment

The extract notes that the parties agree that the surrender of native title is intended to extinguish all native title rights and interests in the agreement area.

Future act provisions

The parties consnet to the surrender of native title rights and interests, over the agreement area, to the State of Queensland.

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The agreement is located within the Waanyi People's area of native title as recognised in the Federal Court of Australia (FCA) proceeding, Aplin on behalf of the Waanyi Peoples v State of Queensland (No 3) [2010] FCA 1515 (FCA file no.: QUD6022/1999; NNTT file no.: QC1999/023)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2017/003"^^xsd:anyURI .

