    schema:description """Kalyeeda Station and Nyikina Mangala Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is a Body Corporate Agreement entered into by:

- Cheryl Marie Camp and Peter James Camp; and

- Walalakoo Aboriginal Corporation.

The Extract fails to outline with any specificity the purpose of the agreement."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6610> ;
    schema:name "Kalyeeda Station and Nyikina Mangala Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2014-011> ;
    schema:startDate "2014-07-04"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the agreement

Commencement

The Agreement commences operation on 4 July 2014, however the Agreement was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT) on 21 October 2014.

No end date for the Agreement is specified.

Native Title Provisions

The Extract notes that the Agreement does not include statements mentioned in subsection 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act.

Background to the ILUA

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Agreement Area falls within the external boundary of Native Title Determination application Nyikina and Mangala (WC1999/025; WAD6099/98).

A Consent Determination was made by the Federal Court on 29 May 2014 in relation to part of the application area (Watson on behalf of the Nyikina Mangala People v State of Western Australia (No 6) [2014] FCA 545)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2014/011"^^xsd:anyURI .

