    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336,
        atns-subcat:51e799aa-68a2-5df5-b3b6-ce3837c24612 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Sand Mining Agreement is a template Future Act Agreement provided by the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT).

It is envisaged by the NNTT that these agreements will be used to assist Indigenous and non-Indigenous Australians to negotiate Future Act Agreements that can be tailored to their specific needs and circumstances.

The Sand Mining Agreement is designed to be used for negotiations between government and a native title party.

The template agreement covers matters including:
(a) permitting the grant of a mining licence; and
(b) stipulating that if a determination that native title exists in the Agreement area is made, the native title party will receive royalties from the conduct of mining under the mining licence."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:dc50c698-80b0-5ef4-bd95-928f2be8da05,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=3410> ;
    schema:name "Sand Mining Agreement"@en ;
    schema:text """The NNTT has issued template agreements covering six categories, being:
1. Future Act Agreements
2. Intra-Aboriginal Agreements
3. Mediation Withdrawal Agreements
4. Negotiating Framework Agreements
5. Pastoral Agreements
6. Reconciliation Agreements Principals.

Please see the ‘Template Agreement’ link at the bottom of this page for further information.

Please see the National Native Title Tribunal's DISCLAIMER in relation to these agreements."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/agreements/files/TemplatesSandMiningFAA/"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:95661c8e-4fe0-54d5-9352-f11daddd56e8 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:4be1244b-2872-5199-8ba6-8c25fb02095d ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:country atns-country:244f6961-729f-5b21-8fc9-baff9dd9af7e ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A003005"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "3381"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:caa3eeb7-4d71-505c-9ee9-19b8c5338435 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """Clarke on behalf of the Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagulk Peoples v State of Victoria [2005] FCA 1795

This is one of three consent determinations to arise out of this case; the other two being Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagulk Peoples No. 1; and Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagulk Peoples No. 3 (see under 'Related Agreements' below).

Between:

Kaylene Pamela Clarke on behalf of the Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagulk Peoples (APPLICANTS) and State of Victoria and others (RESPONDENTS).

Judge: Merkel J

Where made: Horseshoe Bend, Little Desert National Park

Determination:

Native title does not exist.

In relation to the native title claim VID 6005 of 1999, the applicant and respondent parties have agreed that native title does not exist in relation to the Great Western Determination Area (as described in Schedule 1)."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Wimmera, Victoria, Australia"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=3381> ;
    schema:name "Clarke on behalf of the Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagulk Peoples v State of Victoria [2005] FCA 1795 (No.2)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2005-12-13"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """These consent determinations represent the settlement of three native title claims by the Wotjobaluk, Jaadwa, Jadawadjali, Wergaia and Jupagulk Peoples (Wotjobaluk people).

These are the native title claims VID 6002 of 1998, VID 6009 of 1998 and VID 6005 of 1999, located in the Wimmera, in western Victoria.

They were made with the consent of over 400 parties."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.austlii.edu.au/cgi-bin/disp.pl/au/cases/cth/federal%5fct/2005/1795.html"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:956b1d6b-ab02-51b3-b530-81bc4727c6f1 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007759"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7759"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Investigator Road Mooring Buoy Removal Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between MMG Century Limited and the Gulf Region Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate ('RNTBC').

The purpose of the agreement is to consent to MMG Century Limited removing the mooring buoy from the agreement area.

The agreement covers an area of about 6,000 sq m in the seas known as Investigator Road within the South Wellesley Islands, Gulf of Carpentaria.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Carpentaria Land Council Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:endDate "2018-12-22"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7759> ;
    schema:name "Investigator Road Mooring Buoy Removal Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2016-060> ;
    schema:startDate "2016-12-22"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

Agreement Area

The Extract from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements identifies the area subject to this ILUA, per Schedule one of the agreement, as all the land and waters within an area approximately 6,000 sq ms, centred at longitude 139 degrees 54.3 minutes 54.3 seconds East and Latitude 17 degrees 7 minutes 15 seconds South. (Schedule one is attached below under documents).

Commencement:

The agreement operates for a period of two years, from 22 December 2016 until 22 December 2018. It operates as an ILUA from its date of registration, 22 February 2017.

Termination:

The parties agree that no breach of this agreement by any party will give the other party the right to terminate this agreement. The party may exercise any other remedy available to it under the law in respect of a breach.

Some clauses, unspecified in the extract, survive the expiry or termination of the agreement.

Native Title Provisions:

Future act provisions

The parties agree to:

• the removal of the mooring buoy;

• the grant of any interest reasonably required for the removal of the mooring buoy; and

• the doing of anything reasonably required to achieve the above two acts.

The Gulf Region Aboriginal Corporation's consent for the above is subject to substantial compliance by MMG with its obligations under the agreement.

MMG Century Ltd agrees to remove the Mooring Buoy in accordance with the agreed removal process, and to:

• give Gulf Region Aboriginal Corporation at least 30 days written notice of the specific days during which MMG proposes to remove the mooring buoy; and

• to make all reasonable arrangements to facilitate the four Kaiadilt People monitors being present during the removal of the mooring buoy.

Native Title in the Area:

This agreement is located within the native title determination area of the Federal Court of Australia (FCA) proceeding The Lardil Peoples v State of Queensland [2004] FCA 298. (FCA File No.: QUD207/1997, NNTT File No.: QCD2004/001.)"""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2016/060"^^xsd:anyURI .

