    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A008188"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "8188"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Erub Landfill Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between the Torres Strait Island Regional Council, Erubam Le Traditional Land and Sea Owners (Torres Strait Islanders) Corporation RNTBC, Mr Selle Thaiday and the State of Queensland represented by the Department of Natural Resources, Mines and Energy.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for the operation, maintenance, closure, and remediation of the Erub Communtiy Council Tip.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Torres Strait Regional Authority."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=8188> ;
    schema:name "Erub Landfill Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2019-007> ;
    schema:startDate "2019-05-13"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

Commencement and Termination:

The ILUA is binding from the date when signed by all the parties. It has effect as an ILUA and in relation to the agreed acts from the registration date, 13/05/2019. It will continue indefinitely unless terminated by the written agreement of all the parties.Â

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate:

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to the future act provisions of this ILUA.Â

Future act provisions:

The parties agree to certain acts being done, including 'Landfill Related Future Acts'. These include any person doing activities in connection with:Â

• the construction, operation, use, maintenance or repair of the landfill;

• the closure of the landfill; and

• the remediation of the landfill. 'Remediation' of the landfill refers to the measures that are to be completed in order to properly and effectively reverse the environmental effects of the landfill and rehabilitate the agreement area.Â

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The ILUA area is within the area of the the native title determination Mye on behalf of the Erubam Le v State of Queensland [2004] FCA 1573. (FCA file no.: QUD6036/1998, NNTT: QCD2004/005)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2019/007"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:966ba994-eff1-578e-bd49-aff4c5b2c055 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007495"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7495"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Barada Barna People and Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between Central Highlands Regional Council, Isaac Regional Council,
Mackay Regional Council, Les Budby and Cecil Brown Jnr on behalf of the Barada Barna People, and Barada Barna People Aboriginal Corporation on the 29 August 2016.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for certain agreed acts by non-native title parties, relating to the common powers and obligations of local governments.

The agreement area covers about 15,469 sq km, located approximately 60 km south of Mackay in the vicinity of Nebo and Moranbah."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:06f9cf03-2d66-5dfe-807c-b7632b2ea564,
        atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7495> ;
    schema:name "Barada Barna People and Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2016-007> ;
    schema:startDate "2016-08-29"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

The Agreement Area covers about 15,469 sq km, located approximately 60 km south of Mackay in
the vicinity of Nebo and Moranbah.See attached schedule 2 for detailed coordinates of the external boundary of the agreement area.

Commencement

The ILUA commenced on 29 August 2016, and continues indefinitely until the agreement is terminated. The extract does not contain information detailing the manner in which the agreement is to be terminated.

Native Title Provisions

The parties agree that the right to negotiation provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply. The parties also agree that the non-extinguishment principle applies, such that no acts authorised by this agreement will permanently extinguish the native title rights and interests in the agreement area.

The ILUA does have statements that reference subsection 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993(Cth).This mean that the parties consent to the doing of certain agreed acts by the non-native title parties in the future.

The agreed acts are either:

• the low native title impact activities contained in attached schedule 7; or

• the high native title impact activities contained in attached schedule 8, where the local government has either given notice to the relevant native title party about the activity, or has conducted consultation and reached consensus as to the works involving the activity.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The native title determination applications QUD380/2008 and QUD492/2013, to which schedule 2 of this ILUA refers, were determined by consent in the Federal Court of Australia ('FCA') proceedings Budby on behalf of the Barada Barna People v State of Queensland (No 7) [2016] FCA 1271 (NNTT File No.: QCD2016007) and Pegler on behalf of the Widi People of the Nebo Estate #2 v State of Queensland (no 3) [2016] FCA 1272 (NNTT File No.: QCD2016/008) respectively.The ILUA area is within the determination area of Barada Barna People, excluding the determination area of Widi People of the Nebo Estate #2."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2016/007"^^xsd:anyURI .

