    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Port Vincent Marina Indigenous Land Use Agreement enables a marina to be developed at the town of Port Vincent on South Australia's Yorke Peninsula.

Under the Agreement the local Indigenous Narungga People 'acknowledge' that the necessary activities required for the marina development will extinguish native title and they 'surrender any native title rights and interests they may hold in the land.' Without this Agreement, the development would have been invalid and the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) (NTA) would apply. Under the NTA any activity, such as the development, that may affect native title rights is defined as a 'future act' and must otherwise comply with the future act provisions of the NTA in order to be valid."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:dbff1607-a2a3-5baf-995d-8c9bb0552665,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Yorke Peninsula, South Australia, Australia"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=1262> ;
    schema:name "Port Vincent Marina Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2001-07-18"^^xsd:date .

idn-resource:9aeacf14-a169-5238-b4c1-4013c984f79b a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006096"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6096"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Santos-Wongkumara People Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is an area agreement between:
- Santos Ltd (applicant); and
- Clancy McKellar, Iona Dawn Smith, Ernest (Hope) Ebsworth, Rosemary (Rose) Anne Wilson, Margaret Anne Collins, Sharleen Louise Knight, Archie Ebsworth and Noelene Margaret Edwards in their capacity as the Wongkumara Claimants on their own behalf and on behalf of the Wongkumara Native Title Claim Group (the native title claim group for claimant application QUD52/08).

The purpose of this ILUA is provide Santos Ltd with petroleum tenements, approvals and the authority to undertake petroleum activities in the ILUA area."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:7cc37d9a-fe3c-5fec-b115-d1bb8d72db9c,
        atns-sub:81edd075-cb8e-5a7e-a65d-a47cec815898,
        atns-sub:97be12ad-fd1c-5136-9323-0929eb90b556,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6096> ;
    schema:name "Santos-Wongkumara People Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2012-08-03"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

Commencement

The ILUA commences on the commencement date; that is, the day on which the ILUA is executed by all of the parties. It terminates in the event of a contrary determination, if the ILUA is not registered by 5 April 2015, or by mutual agreement of the parties.

Agreement

The Wongkumara claimants consent to:
- the grant of petroleum tenements;
- the grant of approvals; and
- the doing of petroleum activities.

The parties agree that the right to negotiate under the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) does not apply to any future act subject to a consent(those consents given by the Wongkumara Claimants utilized by the petroleum entities to obtain the grant of a petroleum tenement under this ILUA) or the no challenge option.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Wongkumara People People lodged a native title claim on 11 March 2008. Their claim was accepted for registration on 12 April 2008. The area subject to the native title claim covers approximately 50,230 square kilometres of land and is located in the vicinity of Eromanga in south-west Queensland and Tibooburra in north-west New South Wales."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/QLD_-_Registered_ILUA_-_Santos-Wongkumara_People_ILUA_QI2012_073.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:9af82ed2-079a-55f7-a652-c9d8f76a22fa a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A005140"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "5140"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """This ILUA is one of a series of five ILUAs entered into by the Buurabalyji Thalanyji Aboriginal Corporation with pastoral lessees following the determination in Hayes on behalf of the Thalanyji People v The State of Western Australia [2008] FCA 1487 (18 September 2008) dealing with ‘practical co-existence issues between native title holders and pastoralists’ which have been registered after the consent determination (NNTT Media Release).

The Thalanyji and Minderoo Pastoral ILUA was agreed between Murion Cattle Company Pty Ltd (the pastoral lessee of Yanrey Station) and Buurabalyji Thalanyji Aboriginal Corporation (on behalf of the Thalanyji People).

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for the doing of the following future acts:
- the renewal of the subject pastoral lease
- the grant of rights to conduct agricultural activities on the subject pastoral lease
- the grant of rights to conduct 'low impact tourism' in the agreement area
- the extension of the subject pastoral lease or, alternatively, the grant of further pastoral leases to enable pastoralist use of stock routes and reserves"""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:17d993e0-d19e-5349-a48e-4de57b1dba59,
        atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:45d231c6-43e2-507e-b962-39416468877c,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:f630e08a-ea9c-57e3-ab87-066e4b9ad57e,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5140> ;
    schema:name "Thalanyji and Minderoo Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement  (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2010-01-07"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Renewal of the subject pastoral lease

The ILUA provides for the renewal, remaking or re-granting of the subject pastoral lease. This will not effect the rights and interests of the Thalanyji people in the agreement area.

Grant of rights to conduct agricultural activities on the subject pastoral lease

The ILUA enables the pastoralist to grant a licence, permit or authorisation to conduct agricultural activities on the subject pastoral lease. In granting these rights, the pastoralist may grant a right of exclusive occupation which will exclude the Thalanyji people from the areas the subject of the grant.

Grant of rights to conduct 'low impact tourism'

The ILUA provides the pastoralist rights to conduct 'low impact tourism' activities and construct and operate buildings, infrastructure and facilities associated with such tourism. Before such activities are commenced, notice must be provided to the Buurabalyji Thalanyji Aboriginal Corporation.

The ILUA also enables the Buurabalyji Thalanyji Aboriginal Corporation to negotiate with the pastoralist to undertake commercial activties that supplement the tourism activities. Whilst there is no obligation on the pastoralist to accept proposals made in this respect, the pastoralist must undertake negotiations in good faith.

In conducting tourism activities, the pastoralist must respect the Thalanyji People's rights to disseminate information regarding sites of significance and must not use culturally sensitive information.

Stock routes and reserves

The ILUA provides for the pastoralist's continuing right to use stock routes and reserves which are the subject of the agreement. It also provides for occasional grants of pastoral lease tenure over those areas comprising the stock routes and reserves.

General Provisions

The agreement area will reduce where the Thalanyji People's native title rights are compulsorily acquired or where any part of the subject pastoral lease is not renewed or transferred to another party. In the case of a transfer, the agreement area would be unaffected unless the transfer was such that a native title claimant could rely on s 47, 47A or 47B of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) to prevent extinguishment of their native title interests.

The parties agree that their consent to the doing of these acts constitutes the requisite consent for the purposes of ss 24EB(1) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth).

The parties also agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to the grant of the lease.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The ILUA area is located within the Determination Area of native title made in the proceeding Hayes on behalf of the Thalanyji People v The State of Western Australia [2008] FCA 1487 (18 September 2008) by the Federal Court of Australia. The ILUA was signed immediately after the determination, and it was originally contemplated that it would be registered soon after. This ILUA is one of a series of five ILUAs entered into by the Buurabalyji Thalanyji Aboriginal Corporation with pastoral lessees following the determination."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/ILUA%20Register/2009/WI2009.024/ILUARegisterExport.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

