    schema:description """Project: Contract provision of $1.6 million to increase Indigenous employees by 2001
Summary: The DEWRSB Employment Contract relates to the initial provision of aggregated funds to Rio Tinto to support mentor coordinators and prevocational training for Indigenous people. The contract provides for the payment of a placement fee and a fee at the conclusion of 26 weeks' placement for each Indigenous employee placed in full time work and taken off government benefits."""@en ;
