idn-resource:9c81cbd2-ee65-5880-8626-4a3180bfb3bc a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006652"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6652"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Juru People Pretty Bend Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is a Body Corporate Agreement between:

- Londa Cameron Dahl and Peter Leonard Dahl;

- Carol Prior, Raymond Lampton, Colleen Power, Raylene Oui, Tanya Chatfield, Iris Glenbar, Raymond Gaston and Lenora Aldridge (Juru Party); and

-Kyburra Munda Yalga Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC.

The Extract of the Agreement fails to outline with any specificity the purpose of the agreement. However as the Agreement Area is a Pastrol Holding, the purpose is presumably to provide access by means of a lease to the area for pastoral purposes."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6652> ;
    schema:name "Juru People Pretty Bend Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2014-067> ;
    schema:startDate "2014-07-11"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement

The Agreement was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT) on 12 November 2014.

The Extract notes, however, that the Agreement is effective from 11 July 2014, being the date of Native Title Determination in favour of the Juru People.

The Agreement will continue in effect until one of the following events occur:

(a) the Lease term expires; or
(b) surrender, resumption, forfeiture or termination of the Lease; or
(c) the Agreement is removed from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements.

Native Title Provisions

The Extract notes that there are no statements within the Agreement of the kind which are mentioned in 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), and so the consequences set out under these sections are not triggered by this agreement.

This means that the ILUA does not:

- provide consent for the doing of any acts by non-native title parties;

- effect the right of the native title parties to negotiate with non-native title parties proposing to undertake a future act; nor

- validate any previous future acts.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Agreement Area falls within the internal boundary of Native Title Determination application for the Juru People (QC2013/010; QUD544/2010), as accepted for registration 4 March 2014.

In Lampton on behalf of the Juru People v State of Queensland [2014] FCA 736 (11 July 2014) (also known as Juru People(Part A)) it was found by Rares J that native title exists in a significant part of the determination area, but not the entire area claimed by the Juru People, leaving it open for another determination about the remaining parts to be made at a later date."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2014/067"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:9c828738-78b9-5784-b664-fa1154fd95db a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007301"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7301"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Masig (Yorke Island) Defence Facilities ILUA was agreed between the Commonwealth of Australia acting through the Department of Defence, Masigalgal (Torres Strait Islanders) Corporation RNTBC and Torres Strait Island Regional Council on 16 October 2015. The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for a range of acts, whether or not they are 'future acts' regarding the setting up of a body corporate agreement. The agreement area is within the external boundary of the claim area for the Masig People."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:226851a5-4652-58c0-9a88-448bc922deed,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7301> ;
    schema:name "Masig (Yorke Island) Defence Facilities Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2015-085> ;
    schema:startDate "2015-10-16"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement: The ILUA is located in Torres Strait Island Regional Council. The agreement area covers about 730 sq metres on Lease Z in Lot 10 on TS179 Masig (Yorke Island).

Commencement: The ILUA commenced on 16 October 2015.

Native Title Provisions: The ILUA does have statements that reference subsection 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993(Cth).

Background to the Agreement: The ILUA allows a body corporate agreement to be set up between the parties.

Native Title in the ILUA Area: The ILUA is in the native title claim area which includes the land and waters the subject of the Federal Court proceeding Masig People v State of Queensland / Damuth People v State of Queensland [2000] FCA 1067."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2015/085"^^xsd:anyURI .

