RESPONDENT)

Thomas Goodwin Keats (TWENTY-EIGHTH RESPONDENT)

Lorraine Pastoral Co Pty Ltd (TWENTY-NINTH RESPONDENT)

M.D.H Pty Ltd ( (THIRTIETH RESPONDENT)

Robert John McConachy (THIRTY-FIRST RESPONDENT)

Archibald James McDonald (THIRTY-SECOND RESPONDENT)

McMillan Pastoral Company Pty Ltd (THIRTY-THIRD
RESPONDENT)

Catherine Patricial McMillan (THIRTY-FOURTH RESPONDENT)

Harold Henry McMillan (THIRTY-FIFTH RESPONDENT)

William Thomas Mitchell (THIRTY-SIXTH RESPONDENT)

North Australian Pastoral Company Pty Ltd (THIRTY-SEVENTH
RESPONDENT)

Neville Joseph Power (THIRTY-EIGHTH RESPONDENT)

Ronald Arthur Power (THIRTY-NINTH RESPONDENT)

Stanbroke Pastoral Company Pty Ltd (FORTIETH RESPONDENT)

Tom Keats and Co Pty Ltd (FORTY-FIRST RESPONDENT)

Alan James Webber (FORTY-SECOND RESPONDENT)

Judge: Dowsett J

Where made:Mount Isa

Determination:

Native title exists in part of the determination area. It consists of exclusive and non-exclusive native title rights.

Native title is held by the Kalkadoon People.

Exclusive native title rights and interests that exist in the determination area include:
The rights to possession, occupation, use and enjoyment to the exclusion of all others over the determination area identified as exclusive native title.

Non-exclusive native title rights and interests that exist over land in the determination area include:

- the right of access, including the right to camp;
- the right to hunt and to share and exchange traditional natural resourced from the area for personal and domestic purposes;
- the right to conduct cultural and spiritual activities and ceremonies on the area;
- the right to be buried and to bury other Kalkadoon People in the area;
-the right to maintain places of importance and areas of significance and to protect those places and areas from harm;
- the right to teach on the area, the physical and spiritual attributes of the area; and
- the right to hold meetings on the area.

Non-exclusive water rights:

In relation to the native title rights and interests in water within the determination area, the native title holders have the right to hunt, fish, gather, collect and use the Water for personal, domestic and non-commercial communal purposes.

Non-native title rights and interests that exist within the determination area

The rights and interests of the parties under the following Indigenous Land Use Agreements (ILUAs):
- The Kalkadoon People and the State of Queensland under the ï¿½Kalkadoon People/State of Queensland Pre-Determination ILUAï¿½;
- The Kalkadoon people, Mount Isa City and the State of Queensland under the ï¿½Kalkadoon/Mount Isa Northridge Industrial Estate ILUAï¿½; and
- The Kalkadoon people, Mount Isa City and the State of Queensland under the ï¿½Kalkadoon/Gliderport ILUAï¿½.
Further interests include:
- the rights and interests of the State of Queensland, Boulia Shire Council, Burke Shire Council, Cloncurry Shire Council, McKinley Shire Council and Mount Isa Shire Council to access, use, operation, mintainence and control of certain roads in the determination area. The rights and interests of the public to use and access the roads continues.
- The rights and interests of the local government entities (councils to the determination):
(a) under their local government jurisdiction and functions under the Local Government Act 2009 (Qld) and any other legislation;
(b) as the lessor of any leases;
(c) granter of any licenses or other rights and interests;
(d) as the owner and operator of infrastructure, such as roads and pipelines, in the determination area;
(e) under the ILUA with the Kalkadoon People called ï¿½Kalkadoon People and Local Government ILUAï¿½ (note that this does not include Carpentaria Shire Council).
- the rights and interests of Telstra as the owner or operator of telecommunications facilities in the determination area or under legislation;
- The rights and interests of MMG Australia Ltd as the holder of various mining leases, holder of exploration permits and mineral development licenses, under the Dugald River Project Agreement entered into with the Kalkadoon people and interests under the Cultural Heritage Management Plan-Dugald River Project signed with the Kalkadoon People and the Kalkadoon Cultural Heritage Services Pty Ltd;
- The rights and interests of CST Minerals Lady Annie Pty Ltd as the holder of mining leases and exploration permits and interests arising under the agreement with the Kalkadoon people titled ï¿½Lady Annie/Mount Kelly Project ï¿½ Agreement relating to native title and miningï¿½;
- The rights and interests of Roverton Pty Ltd as the owner and operator of gaseous petroleum and associated liquid petroleum distribution facilities within the determination area, as the holder of a pipeline license and holder of a Corridor License;
- The rights and interests of Mount Isa Mines Ltd as the holder of various mining leases, exploration permits and mineral development licences, as the lessee under a pastoral holding, under ILUAs with the Kalkadoon People including Kalkadoon People/Xstrata ILUA, Kalkadoon/MIM ILUA and under the Kalkadoon/MIM Explorer Deed;
- The rights and interests of Noranda Pacific Pty Ltd as the holder of a mining lease, under the McNamaraï¿½s Highway Agreement, under the Cultural Heritage Management Plan-Lady Loretta project ML5568 made with the Kalkadoon People and under the Kalkadoon People/Xstrata ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Xstrata Copper Exploration Pty Ltd as the holder of a mining lease and under the Kalkadoon People/Xstrata ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Ergon Energy Corporation Ltd as the owner and operator of any ï¿½worksï¿½, as a distribution entity and the holder of a distribution authority under the Electricity Act 1994 (Qld). Further rights include rights to any agreement made before the date of determination and the right to enter the determination area to exercise any of the rights or interests referred to above or to inspect, maintain and manage any ï¿½worksï¿½ in the determination area and under the agreement with the Kalkadoon People ï¿½ Kalkadoon People/Ergon ILUA;
- The rights and interests of CS Energy Mica Creek Pty Ltd as the operator of electricity generation and associated facilities including as the operator of Mica Creek Power Station in the determination area, as sub-lessee of a mining lease, as holder of a petroleum pipeline licence, and includes rights of access to exercise the rights referred to above;
- The rights and interests of A A Company Pty Ltd under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Alcala and Canobie ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Argylla Mountains Pastoral Pty Ltd under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Heywood and Murrumba ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Bezuma Pastoral Company Pty Ltd under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Thorntonia ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Cameron Creek Pastoral Company Pty Ltd under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Hillside ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Ian Charles Campbell under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Angus (aka Rosebud) and Coll (aka Rifle Creek) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Graham Curley and Marie Curley under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Bendigo Park (aka Yadthor) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Andrew William Jesse Daniels, Samuel Donald James Daniels and Gabrielle Kennedy under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Roxmere ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Walter George Hacon under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Ballaghmore Downs and Tyndool ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Peter Eric Hacon under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Granada ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Hacon Holdings Pty Ltd under a pastoral development holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Buckingham Downs ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Ronald Leslie Hall under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Gereta and Regent ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Ronald Leslie Hall and Copelan Rose Hall under a term lease and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Gereta and Regent ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Scott Fisher Harrington under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Ibis Creek ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Lionel Albert Hudson under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/ The Nobbies (aka Dugald) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Jersey Plains Pastoral Company Pty Ltd under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Chum Vale, Jersey Plains and Bloodwood ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Thomas Goodwin Keats under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Gleeson ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Alfred Arthur Lanskey under two pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Barr Creek and Toorah Vale ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Edgar Alfred Lanskey under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Bortala (aka Alsace) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of James Lyne Lord and Marjorie Annette Lord under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/May Downs (aka Meltham) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Lorraine Pastoral Company Pty Ltd under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Lorraine/Talawanta ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Robert John McConachy under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Ashover ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Archibald James McDonald under two pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Brightlands and Bulonga ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Donald Francis James McDonald under two pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Farley and Girla (akaGirila) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Harold Henry McMillan under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Carsland, Patricia Vale, Quamby, Evandean, Yambini and Venus (aka Jessivale) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Harold Henry McMilland and Catherine Patricia McMillan under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Carsland, Patricia Vale, Quamby, Evandean, Yambini and Venus (aka Jessivale) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of McMillan Pastoral Company Pty Ltd under pastoral holdings, a term lease and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Corella Park, Ginburra (aka Lanark) Mount Maggie and Tiberu ILUA;
- The rights and interests of MDH Pty Ltd under pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Devoncourt and Stradbroke (aka Stanbroke) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of William Thomas Mitchell under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Bonnockburn (aka Koolamarra) ILUA;
- The rights and interests of the North Australian Pastoral Company Pty Ltd under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Boomara and Coolullah ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Paraway Pastoral Company Pty Ltd under pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Clonagh and Corella ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Ronald Arthur Power and Neville Joseph Power under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Bushy Park ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Stanbroke Pastoral Company Pty Ltd under various pastoral holdings and under the ILUAs made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Stanbroke Kalkadoon State of Queensland ILUA, the Kalkadoon People and Stanbroke and State of Queensland ï¿½ Kamilaroi ILUA;
- The rights and interests Tom Keats and Co Pty Ltd of under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Whites Hill ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Venlock Pty Ltd under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Ardmore ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Alan James Webber under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Mellish Park ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Peter John Woollett and Ann Teresa Woollett under pastoral holdings and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Berguna and Nardoo ILUA;
- The rights and interests of Ivanhoe Colncurry Mines Pty Ltd under a pastoral holding and under the ILUA made with the Kalkadoon People titled the Kalkadoon People/Starcross ILUA;
- The rights and interests of the holders of any permits, claims, licenses, easements, authorities or leases granted under any of the following acts: the Mineral Resources Act 1989 (Qld); the Forestry Act 1959 (Qld); the Land Act 1994 (Qld); and the Water Act 2000 (Qld);
- The rights and interests of the public to undertake any public right to fish or to navigate in the determination area;
- Other interests also include public access rights to waterways, beds and banks of waterways and other public areas that were public before 31 December 1993 in the determination area; and
- Any other rights and interests held by or by reason of law of the Queensland or Commonwealth Governments.

Extinguishment

Areas where native title has been extinguished includes areas of land and waters within the boundaries of the pastoral leases within the determination area on which there has been any permanent improvement consisting of:

- a house, shed or other building;
- an airstrip;
- a dam or other constructed stock watering point or water storage facility; or
- stock yards or trap yards
which have been built before the date of determination in accordance with the rights of the lessee under the pastoral lease.

Native title has also been extinguished over land and waters within mining lease and tenement areas or land that the State of Queensland has taken by proclamation.

Native title has also been extinguished over areas surrendered to the State of Queensland under the Kalkadoon/Mount Isa Northridge Industrial Estate ILUA and the Kalkadoon/Gliderport ILUA.

Provisions Relevant to the Native Title Rights

The Kalkadoon Native Title Aboriginal Corporation, as the prescribed body corporate, is to perform functions required under the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) after becoming registered.

Access to the full text of the determination is available via the URL link."""@en ;
