    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Aurukun Township and Access Road Indigenous Land Use Agreement (the ILUA) allows all future acts in and around the township of Aurukun to be done by the Aurukun Shire Council exempt from the right to negotiate process.

This will allow the Council to carry out works in future without needing to negotiate with the native title claimants, the Wik and Wik-Way People, about each activity. Activities include 'construction, enhancement, maintenance, operation, use [...] repair [...] or access' to public infrastructure, such as roads, reservoirs and drainage, and community works, such as community housing.

However, the Agreement does set out a process for the Council to notify and consult about activities that are to be done in the area of the township that is identified as the 'Undeveloped Area.' The extract from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements explains that Schedule 2 of the ILUA 'comprises notification and consultation processes for future acts proposed to be done on undeveloped areas. The Schedule categorises Future Acts into Minor Future Works and Major Future Works outlining a consultation process for both.'"""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
