    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Yarrabah Towers Indigenous Land Use Agreement is an area agreement between the State of Queensland (Applicant) and Les Murgha on his own behalf and on behalf of the Gunggandji People. The purpose of the agreement concerns infrastructure, communications and the dedication of the agreement area as a conservation park. The commencement and termination date were not specified on the National Native Title Tribunal Register extract (2011)."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:1ec05be0-16ac-52de-bf3b-54bec0211332,
        atns-sub:4f924c21-9e16-51f1-823e-8944b84c7142,
        atns-sub:710c226b-1fba-5eba-86c9-5087f506ac80,
        atns-sub:7cc37d9a-fe3c-5fec-b115-d1bb8d72db9c,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5590> ;
    schema:name "Yarrabah Towers Indigenous Land Use Agreement"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2011-10-04"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Terms of the Agreement
The parties to the Yarrabah Towers ILUA consent to the dedication of the Mt Yarrabah Area and Mt Gorton Area as conservation parks. A conservation park is defined as an area declared as a conservation park under Nature Conservation Act 1992 (QLD).

Background
Native title history
Mr Les Murgha and Mr Stewart Harris, on behalf of the Combined Gunggandji People are currently seeking a determination of native title pursuant to the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth). The claim area lies to the south of Cairns, borders Mission Bay and includes the Yarrabah township. There are numerous respondents including the State of Queensland, Yarrabah Aboriginal Shire Council, Ergon Energy Corporation Limited, Telstra Corporation Limited, numerous fisherman and others. The application was accepted for registration in 2008 having passed the registration test."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/QLD_-_Registered_ILUA_-_Yarrabah_Towers_ILUA_QI2011_015.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

