    schema:description "The Hughenden Framework Agreement was made between the Flinders Shire Council and the Yirandali Native title group. The agreement includes provisions for the recognition of the Yirandali as the area's traditional owners, and aims at developing a cultural heritage management plan for the area. Under the agreement, the 'Yirandali Flinders Forum' was established ensuring regular meetings and information exchange between Yirandali and council representatives."@en ;
