    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Watershed Tungsten Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement was agreed between:

- Vital Metals Limited;

- Graham Brady, Desmond Brickey, Thomas Mitchell, Dell Riley, William Brady, Rodney Riley, Qawanji Ngurrku Jawiyabba Brady, Joseph Cummins, Derrick Henry Oliver, Roy Dennis Levers, Luke Cummins, Alwyn Lyall on their own behalf and for and on behalf of all Western Yalanji People; and

- North Queensland Land Council Aboriginal Corporation.

The purpose of this ILUA is to allow for the grant of application titles and certain future acts on the land, which will enable the development of a mine by Vital Metals."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6082> ;
    schema:name "Watershed Tungsten Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2013-12-13"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Agreement Details
The Parties to this agreement consent to:
(i) the grant of the Application Titles;
(ii) consent to the Future Applications; and
(iii) confirm their consent to all Granted Titles and agree not to challenge the validity of Granted Titles on Native Title or any other basis.

Future Act Agreements
The parties further agree:
(a) to all Future Applications and the Application Titles. This includes agreement to sign documents and do all things that are required by the State or the Miner to facilitate all Future Applications and the grant of the Application Titles in accordance with all applicable laws.
(b) to lodge such documents with the relevant
(c) to consent immediately or agree to any court, tribunal, commission, Minister, adjudicator, official or other competent body
or authority authorising or making determinations that any Future Application and the Application Titles may be granted or carried out and to execute all documents necessary to permit their
grant or occurrence;
(d) not to oppose or make any objections in relation to any Future Application and the Application Titles and,if objections are made contrary to this Agreement, immediately to withdraw those objections upon request by the Miner; and
(e) to the Miner (and an employee, agent or contractor of the Miner) entering the ILUA Area with all necessary vehicles, machinery and equipment to carry out any works or any other activity authorised under a Future Application and the Application Titles and to exercise any other rights conferred by any Interest granted pursuant to a Granted Title, Future Application and the Application Titles.

According to a news report the package negotiated as part of the ILUA includes 'training and education bursaries, employment and small contracting opportunities, and the co-operative application of the local knowledge and experience for the establishment of a dedicated nursery for native trees and vegetation, in preparation for planting and rehabilitation of affected land as operations progress.' (Geological Survey of Iran).

Naive Title in the ILUA Area
Although the Western Yalanji People have been successful in having their rights recognised in two Consent Determinations (Western Yalanji Peoples and Western Yalanji Peoples #3), the land which this ILUA relates to does not fall under either of those determinations. There is currently no active native title claim over the area."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/ILUA%20Register/2012/QI2012.070/ILUARegisterExport.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

