idn-resource:aba62f70-336e-5825-a67c-609687b59d3e a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:eba50e30-5a39-5068-9005-e73af840a07b ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007647"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7647"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Yi-Martuwarra Ngurrara and Christmas Creek Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between Josephine Forrest, Benjamin Laurel, Malcolm Moora, Harry Yungabun, Peter Clancy, Bernadette Williams, Mervyn Numbagardie, Elsie Dickens, Dunba Nunju, Claude Forrest and Sammy Costain on behalf of the Yi-Martuwarra Ngurrara Native Title Group and Klopper Holdings.

The agreement area covers about 359 sq km, situated approximately 75km southeast of Fitzroy Crossing.

The purpose of the ILUA is to consent to access and pastoral activities.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Yanunijarra Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7647> ;
    schema:name "Yi-Martuwarra Ngurrara and Christmas Creek Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2017-017> ;
    schema:startDate "2018-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Background to the Agreement:

This ILUA came about as part of negotiations for the Yi-Martuwarra Ngurrara Native Title Determination when the McGowan Government insisted that an ILUA between Traditional Owners and pastoralists needed to be agreed to before a determination was made. Ultimately, the determination was agreed by consent in the Federal Court of Australia (FCA) proceeding, Forrest on behalf of the Ngurrara People v State of Western Australia (FCA File No.: WAD25/2012; NNTT File No.: WCD2018/001). The State, however, changed its position "at the last minute" about the exclusivity of native title in areas within the Ngurra D part of the claim, and that area was excluded from the determination. Ngurra D, which includes this ILUA area, will have to go through another court process (Yanunijarra Aboriginal Corporation, 2018).

Details of the Agreement:

Commencement:

This Agreement has force as an ILUA from the date of its registration. It has force as a contract on the date that it was executed by all of the parties.

Termination:

This Agreement will end when the Pastoral Lease comes to an end, or when all of the parties agree in writing that it ends. This is except for the obligations arising under clause 17 (not available in the Extract) and the obligations accrued before termination,

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate

The Extract does not contain any statements with respect to the right to negotiate provisions withinSubdivision P, Division 3, Part 2 of the Native Title Act 1992 (Cth). This means that the parties agree that the right to negotiate is maintained.

Future act provisions

The Extract notes that there are no statements within the Agreement of the kind which are mentioned in ss 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), and so the consequences set out under these sections are not triggered. This means that the Agreement does not: provide consent for the doing of any acts by non-native title parties; effect the right of the native title parties to negotiate with non-native title bodies proposing to undertake a future act; nor validate any previous future acts."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2017/017"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:abb42c4c-a0d7-5b00-9759-f9b21d1aee0e a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006225"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6225"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:e25306cd-559a-5d5a-8a28-e66ca2c2323a ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """This Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was entered between the following parties:

- Mantle Mining Corporation Ltd
- Nguddaboolgan Native Title Aboriginal Corporation
- Mt Mulligan Coal Pty Ltd
- Calcifier Industrial Minerals Pty Ltd
- Trafford Coal Pty Ltd
- James Archer, George Archer, Walter Richards Snr, Kenneth Jackson, Lola Brown, Alfred Neal Snr, Percy Neal, Saul Burns Snr,Ernie Burns, Vincent Wason, Maxwell Underwood, Andrew Garrett on their own behalf and on behalf of the Djungan People #1, #2 and #3.

The purpose of this Area Agreement ILUA is to provide consent to Trafford Coal to undertake activities for the discovery, location and delineation of economic coal deposits and payable coal seam gas deposits."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:35e19906-2659-5157-8aee-b9d82eedbb1c,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6225> ;
    schema:name "Indigenous Land Use Agreement relating to EPC772 and ATP718P"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2012-10-03"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

The agreement was entered between the parties so as to provide Trafford, its contractors, servants and agents all the required approvals, consents, licences, titles, renewals and other entitlements so as undertake discovery, location and delineation of economic coal deposits on discovery, location and delineation of economic coal deposits on EPC772 and payable coal seam gas deposits on ATP718P. This agreement does not include mining for commercial extraction of coal and coal seam gas.

Commencement

This agreement commences on 03/10/2012 and continues for the term of the project rights.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Nguddaboolgan Native Title Aboriginal Corporation administers land owned by the Djungan People. The Djungan People’s rights were recognised by the Federal Court of Australia to more than 182,000 hectares of land in North Queensland. The land includes Land Act reserves, pastoral leases and some leasehold and unallocated State Land situated in and around Mount Mulligan, west of Mareeba.

The nature and extent of the native title rights and interests in the area include:
-the right to possess, occupy and enjoy the parts of the land in which exclusive rights exist;
-the right to access, camp on, hunt, fish and gather in the parts of the area in which
non-exclusive rights exist."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/ILUA%20Register/2012/QI2012.090/ILUARegisterExport.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

