    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Yandruwandha/Yawarrawarrka Tinga Tingana Pastoral Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between the State of South Australia (APPLICANT) and Kenneth David Ogilvy and Raylene Patricia Ogilvy; Charlie Moore, Leslie Harris, Fay Nicholls, Theresa Bottrell, Aaron Peterson, Anita Paterson and Fredrick Brown on behalf of the Yandruwandha/Yawarrawarrka People; and the Yandruwandha/Yawarrawarrka Traditional Land Owners (Aboriginal Corporation) on 7 March 2008.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide, amongst other things, for the Yandruwanhda Yawarrawarrka people accessing and undertaking traditional activities in the area covered by the ILUA.

The ILUA was registered on 7 March 2008 and does not have a stipulated period of operation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
