    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Darumbal People, Livingstone Shire Council and Rockhampton Regional Council Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA') is an area agreement that was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal on 23rd of December 2016, under the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between:

• Livingstone Shire Council and Rockhampton Regional Council,

• Alan Douglas Hatfield, Warren John Malone, Rodney William Mann,Vanessa Ross, Amanda Meredith and Pauline Cora on behalf of the Darumbal People; and

• Darumbal People Aboriginal Corporation

The ILUA area covers about 14842.3 sq km located west of Yeppoon approx. 47.5 km north west of Gladstone.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent to a range of Low Native Title Impact Activities, as described in Schedule 7.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area under the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) is Queensland South Native Title Services Ltd."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7660> ;
    schema:name "Darumbal People, Livingstone Shire Council and Rockhampton Regional Council Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA') IN PROGRESS"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2016-024> ;
    schema:startDate "2016-12-23"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

Commencement: The Darumbal People, Livingstone Shire Council and Rockhampton Regional Council Local Government Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA') operates from the Execution Date, and continues unless and until the Agreement is terminated.

Native Title Provisions:

right to negotiate: The Parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to any Future Acts covered by the ILUA.

The Parties agree there are no conditions on the consent to the Low Native Title Impact Activities described in Schedule 7.

future act provision: The Extract notes that there are statements within the ILUA of the kind which are mentioned in 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth). This means that the ILUA provides consent for the doing of the Low Impact Native Title Activities by non-native title parties, as described in Schedule 7.

Native Title in the Area:"""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2016/024"^^xsd:anyURI .

