    schema:description """The Mandandanji People and Roma Clay Target Club Inc Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was entered between the following parties:

- Leslie Weribone, Alexandra Combarngo, David Combarngo, Phyllis Hopkins, Lorraine Tomlinson, Miranda Mailman, Sylvia McCarthy, Violet Costa, Sarah Trindall and Leigh Himstedt on their own behalf and on behalf of the Mandandanji People

- Roma Clay Target Club Inc

- The State of Queensland

The purpose of this area agreement is to provide consent for surrender of native title in the agreement area."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:dbff1607-a2a3-5baf-995d-8c9bb0552665,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6295> ;
    schema:name "Mandandanji People and Roma Clay Target Club Inc Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2013-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

The parties entered into the agreement so as to provide consent to the surrender which will take effect upon registration.

The parties agree to the validating of any
future acts invalidly done by the state in the agreement area prior to registration and that the
acts are valid and are taken to always have been valid.

Commencement

The agreement commences on the commencement date.

Native title provisions

The Right to negotiate is not intended to apply to the surrender.

Native title in the ILUA Area

The Mandandanji people's application to claim native title rights was successfully registered on 06/11/2008."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/ILUA%20Register/2012/QI2012.134/ILUARegisterExport.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

