    schema:description "The Martirendi Agreement is between the City of Salisbury and the Northern Metropolitan Aboriginal Council. It aims to ensure that Indigenous people living in Salisbury participate in all aspects of community life. This is a document of both symbolic significance and of substance. 'Martirende' is a Kaurna Aboriginal word meaning 'to embrace each other'."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:06f9cf03-2d66-5dfe-807c-b7632b2ea564,
        atns-sub:17d993e0-d19e-5349-a48e-4de57b1dba59,
        atns-sub:746b3b59-88ea-5685-81f7-1558875d7c47,
