idn-resource:b5829166-45ae-586d-a6c2-db096d27c90a a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006218"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6218"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The RTIO and Nyiyaparli Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is an Area Agreement between:

• Hamersley Iron Pty Ltd;

• Robe River Mining on its own behalf as a Venturer and as Manager for and on behalf of the Robe River Associates;

• Hamersely HMS Pty Ltd as Manager for and on behalf of the Hope Downs Joint Venturers;

• Hamersely Resources Ltd on its own behalf as a Venturer and as a Manager for and on behalf of the Rhodes Ridge Joint Venturers; and

• David Stock, Gordon Yuline, Raymond Drage, Billy Cadigan and Victor Parker on their own behalf as registered native title claimant and on behalf of the Niyayparli People.

This Area Agreement was registered on 13 March 2013.

The purpose of this agreement is to provide for certain mining activities."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6218> ;
    schema:name "RTIO and Nyiyaparli Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2013-03-13"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

Commencement and Termination

This Agreement commenced on 7 July 2012.

The extract notes that, subject to Clauses 13.3 and 18.3(c) of the Agreement, this ILUA terminates on:

• the termination of the Participation Agreement; and

• the registration of the First ILUA

Where the 'Participation Agreement' is defined as an agreement entered into by RTIO and the Nyiyaparli People on 22 March 2011, and the 'First ILUA' is defined as an agreement entered into by the parties on 28 March 2012.

Consent to Future Acts

For the purposes of s 24EB(1) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), the parties consent to all agreed future acts.

The Right to Negotiate

The right to negotiate provisions in subdivision P of Division 3 of Part 2 of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), do not apply to any agreed act.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Agreement Area covers all the lands and water within the external boundaries of the Nyiyaparli Claimant application (WAD 6280/98 and NNTT No. WC05/6). The claim was registered on 29 November 2005."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/WA_-_Registered_ILUA_-_RTIO_and_Nyiyaparli_ILUA_WI2012_007.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:b58881af-ca3c-547d-a020-791204ba1aa9 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:48b48a3b-3105-596f-b672-832ff76cf4d2,
        idn-resource:53549dc4-f924-5f3a-9307-3bad1bb2c20d,
        idn-resource:fb445242-56be-5980-be02-0d72212eef55 ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A003759"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "3759"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:6ffe90c2-95c9-51b5-a083-8c7d83b975ef ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "The Queensland Agreement on Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health was signed on 23 July 1996 by the Federal Minister for Health and Family Services, Dr Michael Wooldridge, the Queensland Minister for Health, Mr Michael Horan, and the Chairperson of the Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Commission (ATSIC), Ms Lois O'Donoghue."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:d15dd1de-4696-50c8-9f10-2e95eea88e6f,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=3759> ;
    schema:name "Agreement on Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health (Queensland)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "1996-07-23"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """This agreement was among a set of Framework Agreements on Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health entered into by all state and territory governments between July 1996 and February 1999. These were set to expire in June 2000, though the parties agreed to recommit to them and the resigning process began in 2001 (NATSIHC 2003, 23). They were created following an agreement made by state and federal Health Ministers in 1995 to create multilateral framework agreements.

The Framework Agreements were designed to improve coordination between federal and statement governments and to improve relationships between governments and indigenous organisations (NACCHO 1999). Specifically, they aimed ‘to improve health outcomes for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples through:

1. improving access to both mainstream and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander specific health and health related programs which [would] reflect the level of need;
2. increasing the level of resources allocated to reflect the higher level of need of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, including within mainstream services, and transparent and regular reporting for all services and programs; and
3. joint planning processes which [would] inform the allocation of resources and allow for:
• full and formal Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander participation in decision making and determination of priorities;
• improved co-operation and co-ordination of current service delivery; and
• increased clarity with respect to the roles and responsibilities of the key stakeholders.’ (NACCHO 1999).

Following the creation of the first set of Framework Agreements, a national level agreement was created (the National Strategic Framework for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health). The first state and territory Framework Agreements have since been re-signed or replaced under this national framework.

This Agreement was replaced initially by the Agreement on Queensland Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health (2002) and then by the Agreement on Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Service Delivery between the Commonwealth of Australia and the Government of Queensland (2005)."""@en .

