    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Framework Agreement between the Native Title Claimants, the Rubibi Working Group and the State of Western Australia was signed in early 1998 prior to the amendments to the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) in mid 1998.

The Framework Agreement was intended to lead to a Final Agreement and establishes a working relationship between the parties. It also identifies the substantive issues for negotiation, the negotiators, and the negotiation procedures for a Final Agreement."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:17d993e0-d19e-5349-a48e-4de57b1dba59,
        atns-sub:51ca8813-b7bb-5a37-819e-afae35771fff,
        atns-sub:5996de0c-8cc6-5f14-8901-d839af36a4d4,
        atns-sub:746b3b59-88ea-5685-81f7-1558875d7c47,
        atns-sub:9e5e8f61-69be-5e2a-a9cd-58fb000349bd,
        atns-sub:b39d3bcb-b425-5b5d-b1f1-9735a7a6a23b,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "Shire of Broome, Western Australia, Australia"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=1803> ;
    schema:name "Framework Agreement between the Native Title Claimants, the Rubibi Working Group and the State of Western Australia"@en ;
    schema:startDate "1998-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The issues identified for negotiation include:
- Economic development of the Broome Aboriginal Community;
- Operation of State Law;
- Interim Agreement with the Shire of Broome;
- Ratification Procedures;
- Differing Entitlements;
- Waterbank Lease;
- Neighbourhood A Subdivision;
- Horticultural Leases;
- Proposed Racecourse Resort Development;
- Cultural and Environmental Coastal Zones;
- Dampier Creek and Fishermans Bend;
- Crocodile Farm;
- Yardoogarra Reserve;
- Existing Aboriginal Land;
- Access to Crown Land;
- Cultural and Heritage Protection;
- Wattle Downs Special Purpose Lease; and
- General Provisions."""@en .

