idn-resource:c486cac6-a8f5-50d9-98e6-80cd3bf94fb9 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007247"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7247"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Wulli Wulli People/Wondekai Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA') was agreed under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) between the Wulli Wulli People and the Wondekai.

The agreement area is about 24 sq km, located approximately 34 km south of Theodore. The local government area is the Banana Shire Council.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for a range of acts, whether or not they are 'Future Acts', regarding the access to and use of the land subject to pastoral leases.

The agreement area is located within the external boundary of the Wulli Wulli People native title claim. The Wulli Wulli Claim was filed on 17 July 2000. It covers an area of approximately 5,432 square kilometres and includes the towns of Theodore and Cracow, pastoral properties, Precipice & Isla Gorge National Parks, state forests and sections of the Dawson River.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is Queensland South Native Title Services Ltd."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:8afa6040-57f6-5faf-a4f9-863bd8f4f470,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7247> ;
    schema:name "Wulli Wulli People/Wondekai Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2016-01-29"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of Agreement:

Agreement area: The extract of the ILUA from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements describes the area covered by the agreement as follows: the area subject to this agreement covers all land and waters subject to: Lot 5019 on PH52. It covers about 24 sq km, located about 34 km south of Theodore.

Commencement: This ILUA commenced on 29 January 2016.

Native Title Provisions: The ILUA does not have statements that reference subsection 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth).

Native Title in the ILUA Area:

The ILUA is in the native title claim area which includes the land and waters the subject of Federal Court Proceedings QUD 6006 of 2000. It is one of six agreements which were subject to a conditional determination by the Federal Court of Australia on 13 August 2015 (QUD6006/2000) and later subject to a consent determination by the Federal Court of Australia on 18 July 2017."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/ILUA%20Register/2015/QI2015.077/ILUARegisterExport.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

