idn-resource:c8241f99-959c-5bc9-9490-1d3699fb9a4a a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A008803"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "8803"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Strelley Nyamal Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) (NTA), between the Nyamal Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate (RNTBC) and Pinga Pty Ltd; Strelley Pastoral Pty Ltd; Nomads Charitable and Educational Foundation Inc; the Strelley Housing Society Inc; and the Coongan Aboriginal Corporation.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide the Nyamal People's consent to the Coogan and Strelley Pastoral Leases, the PInhga and Strelley Social Housing Leases, as well as to authorise agricultural activities

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Yamatji Marlpa Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:45d231c6-43e2-507e-b962-39416468877c,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=8803> ;
    schema:name "Strelley Nyamal Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2020-012> ;
    schema:startDate "2000-11-17"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Background to the Agreement [IF NO INFORMATION AVAILABLE, DELETE THIS HEADING]

Details of the Agreement

Commencement and Termination

The ILUA has force as a contract from the date when signed by all the parties. It has effect and as an ILUA, an in relation to the agreed future acts, from its registration date.

The ILUA will end when any one of the following occurs:

• the last of the pastoral leases and special leases come to an end;

• the Nyamal People are no longer recogniseda snative title holders to the ILUA area; or

• by the written mutual agreement of the parties.

Native Title Provisions

Right to negotiate

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the NTA do not apply.

Extinguishment

The parties agree that the non-extinguishment principle applies. This means that under s 24EB(3) of the NTA any of the activities authorised under this ILUA which may be inconsistent with native title rights and interests do not extinguish these rights and interests, instead they are revived when the activities are finished.

Future act provisions

The Nyamal People agree to the following future acts:

• the continuance or replacement of the Coogan and Strelley Pastoral leases from time to time;

• the continuance or replacement of the Pinga and Strelley Housing Special Leases from time to time, provided the terms do not change in any substantial way;

• the granting of a authorisations from time to time to conduct agricultural activities on the Pastoral Leases.

Native Title in the Agreement Area

The ILUA area is within the determination area of the Nyamal People #1 and the whole of the GEI134817 lease area where native title exists in NYamal #10."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2020/012"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:c82d542c-aeb3-5ac3-a0e6-63d5ee6ab90b a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A005910"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "5910"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Jangga/Urella Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between:

- Dale Gordon Francis Dennis and Lorissa Dennis (applicant); and

- Bulganunna Aboriginal Corporation

on 25 November 2013.

The purpose of this Body Corporate ILUA is to grant consent regarding pastoral activities within the Agreement Area."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5910> ;
    schema:name "Jangga/Urella Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2013-069> ;
    schema:startDate "2013-11-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

The ILUA was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT) on 25 November 2013.

The Extract does not specify specific start or end dates for the Agreement.

However, the Extract does note that the Agreement takes effect on the Date of Determination of Native Title in favour of the Jangga People, being 9 October 2012.

The Agreement will continue in effect until:

(a) the Lease term expires; or
(b) the date of surrender, resumption, forfeiture or termination of the Lease; or
(c) the date upon which the Agreement is removed from the Register of ILUAs.

The Extract does not include extensive information regarding the terms of the Agreement.

Native Title Provisions

The Extract notes that there are no statements within the Agreement of the kind which are mentioned in 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth).

This means that the ILUA does not:

- provide consent for the doing of any acts by
non-native title parties;

- effect the right of the native title parties to negotiate with non-native title parties proposing to undertake a future act; nor

- validate any previous future acts.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

On 9 October 2012, the Federal Court of Australia recognised the Jangga People’s Native Title rights and interests over approximately 11,350 square kilometres of land in Central Queensland. The decision of McLennan on behalf of the Jangga People v State of Queensland [2012] FCA 1082 effectively reaffirms the Jangga People’s affinity with their traditional lands around Mount Coolon, Urella and Lake Dalrymple."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2013/069"^^xsd:anyURI .

