    schema:description """Juru Protected Area Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is a Body Corporate Agreement between:

- State of Queensland, Department of Natural Resources and Mines;

- Carol Prior, Raymond Lampton, Colleen Power, Raylene Oui, Tanya Chatfield, Iris Glenbar, Raymond Gaston and Lenora Aldridge on their own behalf and on behalf of the Juru People; and

- Kyburra Munda Yalga Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC.

The Extract does not provide extensive information regarding the purpose of the Agreement."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:7cc37d9a-fe3c-5fec-b115-d1bb8d72db9c,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6734> ;
    schema:name "Juru Protected Area Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2014-074> ;
    schema:startDate "2014-08-29"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement

This ILUA was registered with the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements on 18 December 2014.

The Extract does not provide a specific start or end date for the Agreement.

The Extract does note, however, that Clauses 1 - 4 and 12 commence on the Execution Date, being 29 August 2014.

The remaining Clauses of the Agreement commence on the Determination Effect Date, being 11 July 2014.

The Agreement will continue in force for a period of twenty (20) years.

Native Title Provisions

The Extract notes that there are no statements within the Agreement of the kind which are mentioned in 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), and so the consequences set out under these sections are not triggered by this agreement.

This means that the ILUA does not:

- provide consent for the doing of any acts by non-native title parties;

- effect the right of the native title parties to negotiate with non-native title parties proposing to undertake a future act; nor

- validate any previous future acts.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Agreement Area includes all of the land and waters within that part of Lot 141 on Plan NPW 1152 located within the Native Title Determination application QUD554 of 2010 Juru People (QC2013/010)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2014/074"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:cc515110-3521-5f3b-bb4c-5edf4bbcaf20 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
