    atns:sourceEntityId "7999"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Yungnora Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate ('RNTBC'), Buru Energy Limited and Diamond Resources (Canning) Pty Ltd Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA') was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between Yungnora Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC, Buru Energy Ltd, and Diamond Resources (Canning) Pty Ltd.

The agreement area covers about 1,768 sq km, in the vicinity of Noonkanbah extending north of the Fitzroy River.

The purpose of the agreement is to provide consent for the Buru/Diamond Resources (Canning) petroleum exploration and operation project.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Kimberley Land Council Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:35e19906-2659-5157-8aee-b9d82eedbb1c,
        atns-sub:81edd075-cb8e-5a7e-a65d-a47cec815898,
        atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7999> ;
    schema:name "Yungngora Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC, Buru Energy Limited and Diamond Resources (Canning) Pty Ltd Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/WI2016-011> ;
    schema:startDate "2016-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Agreement area:

The agreement area covers about 1,768 sq km, in the vicinity of Noonkanbah extending north of the Fitzroy River.

The extract from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements identifies the area subject to this ILUA, per schedule 1 of the agreement (attached to the extract below), as all the land and waters within the Noonkanbah Pastoral Lease Area (Lot 255 on Plan DP220190), an Unclaimed Crown Land Lot that is wholly within the Noonkanbah Pastoral Lease Area, and the part of Reserve 23266 (Stock Route) that lies within the westernmost and easternmost boundaries of the Noonkanbah Pastoral Lease Area. The agreement excludes the area within the Noonkanbah Pastoral Lease Area known as "Umpampurr", "Pea Hill Hay Paddock" or the "Pilot Site".

Commencement:

The agreement commenced on 5 September 2016, that being the date that the agreement had been signed by all the parties.

Termination:

No end date is specified in the extract.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to any Project Title or Approval agreed to under this ILUA.

Extinguishment

Any acts done by the non-native title parties under this agreement will not extinguish native title rights and interests.

Future act provisions

The parties consent to the granting of the agreed Project Titles and Approvals. The Project involves exploring for petroleum and includes extracting, producing, refining, or transporting petroleum pursuant to the Titles and any lawful activities in connection with the Project Titles.

Background to the Agreement:

Buru and Diamond are equal joint partners under the "Joint Operating Agreement - Exploration Permit EP 371" dated 13 April 2011.

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The agreement is within the area of native title recognised in the Noonkanbah determination, Cox on behalf of the Yungngora People v State of Western Australia [2007] FCA 588 (FCA file no.: WAD6229/1998; NNTT file no.: WCD2007/002)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=WI2016/011"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:ceb80553-fc51-5a91-a618-f5a99f09b8c5 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006301"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6301"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Pitta Pitta People/Bengeacca and Stockport Indigenous Land Use Agreement(ILUA)was entered into between the following parties:

- Reginald Hasted Beauchamp and Vida Felicia Beauchamp

- Alfred Nathan, Jean Jacks, Neville Aplin, Carmel Belford, Noel Doyle and Florence Melville on behalf of the Pitta Pitta People.

The purpose of the area agreement is to specify access arrangements to the pastoral property, Stockport."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6301> ;
    schema:name "Pitta Pitta People/Bengeacca and Stockport Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2013-08-05"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

As per the agreement, the agreement takes effect on the date that a determination of native title in favour of the Pitta Pitta People is made, and continues until:
- the date of expiry of the lease term
- the date of surrender, resumption, forfeiture or termination of the lease
- the date of removal of the Agreement from the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements

Native title in the ILUA Area

The native title rights of the Pitta Pitta people was recognised on 28 August 2012 over 66 parcels of land near Boulia in the consent determination of Aplin on behalf of the Pitta Pitta People v State of Queensland [2012] FCA 883. The claim area included approximately 30,000 square kilometres near the Queensland/Northern Territory border and about 200 kilometres south of Mt Isa. The determination area is centred on the township of Boulia and includes land in the shire councils of Boulia, Cloncurry, Diamantina and Winton. It covers low lying plains in the Channel Country and the Burke, Hamilton and Georgina Rivers. The area enjoys a warm, semi-arid climate. Thus waterholes and watercourses were, and are an important part of the relationship between the people and the land.

The non-exclusive native title rights that were recognised in relation to land include:
- the right to access and camp on the area;
- the right to hunt and gather on the area for non-commercial, personal, domestic, social, cultural and communal purposes;
- the right to take and use natural resources from the area for non-commercial purposes;
- the right to maintain places of importance and areas of significance to the Native Title Holders under their traditional laws and customs and protect those places and areas from physical harm;
- the right to conduct ceremonies on the area;
- the right to teach the physical and spiritual attributes of the area; and
- the right to light fires on the area for domestic purposes including cooking, but not for the purpose of hunting or clearing vegetation.

In relation to water in parts of the Determination Area the following non-exclusive rights apply:
- to hunt, fish and gather from the water for personal, domestic, social, cultural and non-commercial communal purposes; and
- to take and use the water for personal, domestic and non-commercial communal purposes."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/ILUA%20Register/2013/QI2013.021/ILUARegisterExport.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:cec1b53c-6427-5c4d-95cd-2f65a9cf99d6 a atns:Entity ;
