idn-resource:cecf7c0c-6a8c-5453-86c5-14bb8d820dcc a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:references idn-resource:7b928a0d-47c5-537a-9136-066ae7f542f4 ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:country atns-country:244f6961-729f-5b21-8fc9-baff9dd9af7e ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A000821"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "1298"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description "This Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between Ausquest Limited and the Central Land Council. The purpose of this ILUA was to allow mineral exploration by Ausquest, in line with the Exploration Licences it had been granted over two areas located west and north of Lajamanu."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:17d993e0-d19e-5349-a48e-4de57b1dba59,
        atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:35e19906-2659-5157-8aee-b9d82eedbb1c,
        atns-sub:746b3b59-88ea-5685-81f7-1558875d7c47,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:e52a2091-dcda-569c-aafb-6497428c615c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:location "West and north of Lajamanu, Northern Territory, Australia"@en ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=1298> ;
    schema:name "Ausquest Limited/CLC Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2001-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Contents of this ILUA

This ILUA enabled four Exploration Licence (EL) applications to be granted, also validating any future exploration activity in the area. Without this ILUA, the grant of the ELs may have been invalid, or it may have attracted the right to negotiate and the future act provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth).

The native title holders were represented by the Central Land Council in this ILUA. Their consent to the exploration was given subject to certain conditions. Accordingly, the ILUA included several conditional provisions regarding:

• 'procedures to minimise the environmental impact of exploration and to promote the rehabilitation of any part of the Area which has been subjected to exploration;'

• 'the protection of any native title rights and interests, including the protection of sacred sites;' and

• compensation.

Removal from the Register

This ILUA has now been removed from the National Native Title Tribunal Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements. It was removed under s 199C(1)(c)(i) of the Native Title Act 1993, which allows the removal of an ILUA from the Register if a party advises the Registrar in writing that the agreement has expired, and the Registrar believes, on reasonable grounds, that it has expired."""@en .

idn-resource:cedbbaee-f435-53ca-ae82-bfeafb28f032 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A006732"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "6732"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """Bulganunna Aboriginal Corporation and Adani Mining Carmichael North Galilee Basin Rail Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is a Body Corporate Agreement between:

- Adani Mining Pty Ltd;

- Bulganunna Aboriginal Corporation RNTBC; and

- State of Queensland, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Land Services, Department of Natural Resources and Mines.

The purpose of the Agreement is to provide consent for Project Activities, including Future Acts, to occur within the Agreement Area."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6732> ;
    schema:name "Bulganunna Aboriginal Corporation and Adani Mining Carmichael North Galilee Basin Rail Project Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2014-065> ;
    schema:startDate "2014-08-06"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Commencement

This ILUA was registered with the Register of Indigenous Land Use Agreements on 5 January 2015.

The Extract does not provide a specific start or end date for the Agreement.

The Extract does note, however, that the Agreement commences on the Execution Date, being 6 August 2014. The Agreement will operate for the duration of the Project Activities.

Native Title Provisions

Future Acts

The Parties to the Agreement consent to:

(a) all Future Acts and Surrenders necessary for the construction, operation and maintenance of up to three (3) Rail Corridors;
(b) any other Surrender that is necessary for the Project to proceed. This may include where Adani (or any Related Bodies Corporate or third party or parties nominated by Adani) requires a Grant or Grants of fee simple, perpetual lease or other tenure
wholly inconsistent with the continuation of Native Title;
(c) the Project Activities (including the doing of all Future Acts and the validating of any Future
Acts undertaken after the Execution Date that would otherwise have been invalid); and
(d) all Future Acts that are necessary for the construction, operation and maintenance of the Quarry Sites.

Surrender

The Parties to the Agreement acknowledge that the Surrender is intended to extinguish any Native Title existing in relation to the Surrender Area at the time of the Surrender.

Right to Negotiate

The Parties to the Agreement agree that the Right to Negotiate does not apply to any Project Activities or any Surrender covered by the Agreement.

Project Activities

The Project Activities include all acts (including Future Acts) necessary for the Project. This includes all acts executed by, for, on behalf of or for the benefit of Adani or any Related Bodies Corporate of Adani or any third party or third parties nominated by Adani which are necessary for investigating, implementing,
developing, constructing, installing, operating, maintaining, repairing, replacing, further developing and decommissioning the Project within, or in relation to, the Agreement Area including:
(a) the construction, operation and maintenance of up to three Rail Corridors;
(b) the construction, operation and maintenance of a Power Corridor;
(c) the construction, operation and maintenance of roads, haul roads, bridges, groin walls, electricity transmission lines, telecommunication lines, communication facilities, quarries,
borrow pits, laydown areas, stockpiles, water pipelines, gas pipelines, sewerage pipelines, other utility infrastructure, navigational equipment or aids, office or accommodation buildings, camps and any other building or structures necessary for the Project;
(d) the clearing, management and rehabilitation of lands and waters and any flora and fauna contained therein;
(e) Surrenders;
(f) Grants of Approvals; and
(g) works comprising or associated with the matters referred to in paragraphs (a) to (f) of this definition.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The ILUA Area covers all land and waters within the Native Title determination QUD6230/98 Jangga People (QCD2012/009)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2014/065"^^xsd:anyURI .

