    schema:description """The Warraber Island Primary Health Care Centre Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between the State of Queensland (APPLICANT), the the Warraberalgal (Torres Strait Islanders) Corporation and Ian Larry on 11 March 2008.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide for construction works and the grant of a Trustee Lease.

The ILUA was registered on 11 March 2008, and does not have a stipulated period of operation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=4566> ;
    schema:name "Warraber Island Primary Health Care Centre Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2008-03-11"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """The parties to the ILUA consent:

- to construction acts and the grant of the Trustee Lease taking place without objection or opposition from the Warraberalgal People;

- that no compensation is payable in relation to the construction acts or grant of the Trustee Lease;

- that, as far as is applicable, the non-extinuishment principle applies to the construction acts and the grant of the Trustee Lease."""@en .

