    schema:name "Land Use and Access Agreement between Western Yalanji, State of Queensland and Noel A. Adam"@en ;
    schema:startDate "1998-09-28"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Adam had mining interests in parts of the determination area and had applied for three mineral exploration permits over land the subject of the determination. Pursuant to the Agreement, if those mineral exploration permits were granted by the Minister responsible for the Mineral Resources Act 1989, then Western Yalanji authorised those permits to be granted. In addition Western Yalanji authorised the continued use by Adam of the existing Horn Valley airstrip and the roads and tracks within the determination area in relation to his mining and exploration interests. The Western Yalanji also authorised the construction, maintenance and use by Adam of a water reticulation system to allow Adam to transport water from the Mitchell River to any mining sites for the purposes of mining activities. Construction of any part of the water reticulation system or of any new or re-routed road or track within the determination area was subject to written clearance by Western Yalanji concerning the presence of sites of significance.

The Agreement does not affect the rights of the Western Yalanji to claim compensation from the State of Queensland pursuant to the Native Title Act 1993 and from Adam pursuant to the Mineral Resources Act 1989. Neither does it affect the rights of the State to claim compensation from Adam pursuant to the Mineral Resources Act 1989. The Agreement also sets out a dispute resolution process."""@en .

idn-resource:d71dc584-0be4-504c-b8ed-3b36038c5533 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A007676"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "7676"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The ful name of this agreement is the Northern Gas Pipeline: Central Land Council (CLC) Tennant Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA). It was made under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) between:

• Jemena Northern Gas Pipeline Pty Ltd;

• the Central Land Council; and

• the Northern Territory of Australia.

The agreement area covers approx. 21 sq km of land comprised of a 750m wide corridor that extends approx. 29 km eastward from a point commencing about 25 km east of the Three Ways Roadhouse and ending at a point about 54 km east of Three Ways Roadhouse.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for the development of the Northern Gas Pipeline in the agreement area.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Central Land Council."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:51ca8813-b7bb-5a37-819e-afae35771fff,
        atns-sub:81edd075-cb8e-5a7e-a65d-a47cec815898,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7676> ;
    schema:name "Northern Gas Pipeline: CLC Tennant Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/DI2017-005> ;
    schema:startDate "2017-04-07"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

Commencement:

The agreement operates from 7 April 2017.&

Termination:

The agreement will terminate on the date that the Principal Agreement terminates, unless terminated earlier in accordance with clause 6.6(b) of the agreement. The Extract does not include the text of this clause.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply with respect to the agreed acts.

Future act provisions

The Extract notes that there are statements within the agreement of the kind which are mentioned in ss 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act1993(Cth), and so the consequences set out under these sections are triggered. This means that the agreement provides consent for the doing of certain acts by the non-native title parties.Specifically the agreement provides consent for the doing of the following acts:

• the validating of all acts done invalidly prior to the registration of this agreement;

• the grant of the pipeline licence, meaning any licence granted to Northern Gas Pipeline Pty Ltd persuant to s 15 of the Energy Pipelines Act 1981 (NT) in response to the application (initial licence), and any substitution, renewal or extension of the initial licence provided that no rights different to that created by the initial licence are created;

• the grant of any right, title or interest in respect of the pipeline or the Project;

• the grant of tenure;

• the conduct of the activities;

• the operation of the pipeline; and

• all acts necessary or incidental to the above acts or to the implementation of the Project provided that such acts have no greater effect on native title than any of the above acts.

The pipeline is specified as being a single approx. 622 km buried high pressure gas pipeline with a nominal diameter of approx. 12 iinches from the Amadeus Gas Pipeline near Tennant Creek to the Carpentaria Gas Pipeline near Mt Isa"""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=DI2017/005"^^xsd:anyURI .

