    schema:description "The Lambina Opal Mining Field Agreement was signed by the South Australian Opal Miners Association and the traditional owners of the area. The agreement allows miners to enter and mine the Lambina area, and offers traditional owners 'noodling' rights. All miners taking up claims in the Lambina must adhere to conditions protecting traditional sites and waterholes and ensure rehabilitation of mined land."@en ;
