    schema:description "The Angus Downs Joint Management Financial Assistance Agreement (the Agreement) is an agreement in relation to funding for the proposed Angus Downs Joint Management Indigenous Protected Area (IPA). The parties to the Agreement are the Commonwealth of Australia and the Parks and Wildlife Commission of the Northern Territory (PWCNT). Since 2001 funding has been provided in relation to the proposed IPA on a yearly basis through the Natural Heritage Trust for the purposes of: consultation with Traditional Owners and those having an interest in Angus Downs; the establishment of a steering committee; the development of a draft plan of management; and development of a draft framework agreement between the Traditional Owners and PWCNT. The Agreement was varied by a Deed of Agreement of 9 April 2002 which replaced the scope of the work to be undertaken and replaced the proposed budget."@en ;
