    atns:sourceEntityId "7686"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2,
        atns-subcat:177cef4d-1963-57e3-9b5c-508480daf336 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Tanami Gas Pipeline: Napperby Perpetual Pastoral Lease Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA') was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal on 29/10/2018, under the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between:

• AGI Tanami Pty Limited;

• Ngalyia Aboriginal Corporation Registered Native Title Body Corporate ('RNTBC');

• Central Land Council; and

• Northern Territory of Australia.

The ILUA area covers about 6.32 sq km and is located adjacent to and north of Tanami Road in the Tilmouth Crossing area, about 328 km north west of Alice Springs.Â

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent for Pipeline licensing and development of the pipeline.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is the Central Land Council."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:81edd075-cb8e-5a7e-a65d-a47cec815898,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=7686> ;
    schema:name "Tanami Gas Pipeline: Mt Doreen Perpetual Pastoral Lease Indigenous Land Use Agreement ('ILUA')"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/DI2018-007> ;
    schema:startDate "2018-10-29"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

Commencement:

This ILUA commenced operating on the 16 May 2018.Â

Termination:

This ILUA will terminate on the date the Principal Agreement titled 'Benefits and Impact Agreement: Tanami Gas Pipeline' comes to an end.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) are not intended to apply to the doing of any or all of the relevant acts in the ILUA.Â

Future act provisions

The extract notes that there are statements within the ILUA of the kind which are mentioned in ss24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), and so the consequences set out under these sections are triggered. This means that the ILUA provides consent for the doing of certain acts by the non-native title parties. Specifically the ILUA provides consent for the doing of the following acts:

• the grant of the Pipeline Licence;

• the grant of any right, title or interest in respect of the Pipeline or the Project;

• the grant of tenure;

• the conduct of Activities;

• the operation of the pipeline; and

• any and all acts necessary or incidental to the Relevant Acts or to the implementation of the Project provided that such acts have no greater effect on native title than any of the acts done in accordance with the above.Â

Native Title in the Area:

This ILUA is located within the native title determination area recognised by the Federal Court of Australia ('FCA') proceeding Napangardi on behalf of the members of Jiri/Kuyukurlangu, Kampu,
Kunajarrayi, Mikanji, Pikilyi, Pirrpirrpakarnu, Wantungurry,
Wapatali/Mawunji, Warlukurlangu, Yamaparnta, Yarripiri and Yarungkanyi/Murrku Estate Groups v Northern Territory of Australia [2013] FCA 637. (FCA File No.: NTD39/2011, NNTT File No.: DCD2013/002)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=DI2018/007"^^xsd:anyURI .

