    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Rocks Quarry Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed, under the provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), between:

• Colevale Estates Pty Ltd,

• M & T Populin Pty Ltd,

• Twin Rock Pty Ltd and

• Allec Illin, Eddie Smallwood, Della Gibson, Jasmine Stanley, Christine Skeene, Eddie Savage, Fred Stanley Snr., Marlene Singleton, Kim Neal on their behalf and on behalf of Bindal People #2.

The ILUA area covers approx 4 sq. km and is located approx 17 km southwest of Ayr along Ayr-Dalbeg road.

The purpose of the ILUA is to provide consent to all activities relating to quarrying project in the ILUA area.

The Native Title Representative Body for this area is North Queensland Land Council Native Title Representative Body Aboriginal Corporation."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=8143> ;
    schema:name "The Rocks Quarry Indigenous Land Use Agreement"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2019-020> ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement:

The ILUA area is as per map attached in Schedule 1 of the ILUA. The ILUA area is described as Lot 18 on SP SP178779 and Lot 122 on SP SO178779.

Commencement and Termination:

The agreement commences on the date when all parties have signed the agreement; and can be terminated in a way provided in the clause 3.2 of the ILUA. The way of termination is not included in the extract. In case of a breach, remedies at law may be available to parties.

Native Title Provisions:

Right to negotiate:

The right to negotiate under the Native Title Act 1993 does not apply to any Project Activities covered by the ILUA.

Future act provisions:

The parties agree to following activities in relation to the Quarrying Project:

• amending or varying existing Sales Permit in a way that removes any Native Title Restriction;

• re-issuing any existing Sales Permit in a way that removes any Native Title Restriction;

• issuing any new Sales Permit in a way that removes any Native Title Restriction; and

• all future acts done in relation to the Quarrying Project.

Quarrying Project means:

• the exploration for and extraction of Quarry material;

• the collection and transportation of Quarry material;

• the stockpiling and storage of Quarry material; and

• use of Quarry material in any value adding process.

Native Title in the Agreement Area:

The ILUA area is within the area of the Native Title Application made by Allec Illin & Ors on the behalf of Bindal People #2 v State of Queensland (Bindal People #2) (NNTT file number QC2016/005; Federal Court file number QUD503/2016)."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2019/020"^^xsd:anyURI .

