        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        atns-sub:dbff1607-a2a3-5baf-995d-8c9bb0552665,
        atns-sub:eb0505b2-1a8a-50e0-81ae-843a12f07744,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6870> ;
    schema:name "Barry Fisher & Ors on behalf of the Ewamian People #2 v State of Queensland & Ors"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2013-11-26"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Background
About 26,000 square kilometres in Gulf country was recognised as belonging to the Ewamian people. The recognition of native title will open up the opportunity for the legacies of the region’s traditional owners to continue.

Details of Judgement
Through mediation, agreement has been reached as to the terms of a determination of native title to provide recognition of the native title rights and interests held by the Ewamian People in relation to part of the land and waters covered by the Ewamian People Application. The signed agreement was then filed in the Federal Court pursuant to s 87 of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth). The court was satisfied that a determination of native title was within the power of the court."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/NNTR_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QCD2013/006"^^xsd:anyURI .

