    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The APLNG and Iman People Fairview and Eurombah Creek Projects Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) is an Area Agreement between:

- Australia Pacific LNG Pty Limited & Australia Pacific LNG CSG Transmissions Pty Limited (individually and collectively, APLNG) (applicant); and

- Richard Doyle, Patrick Silvester, Kenny Waterton, Eve Fesl, Eddie Waddy, Graham Anderson, Arwa Waterton, Cynthia Kemp, Bradley
Curtis, Dena Marie Dodd-Ugle, Heidi Anne-Marie Lawson on behalf of the Iman People #2 native title determination application (Iman People)

The purpose of this Area Agreement is to authorise the undertaking of the Fairview Pipeline Project and Eurombah Creek Lateral Project on the land covered by the ILUA."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:3302d162-15ce-5b7d-ad89-1f11c3cb6e0d,
        atns-sub:51ca8813-b7bb-5a37-819e-afae35771fff,
        atns-sub:81edd075-cb8e-5a7e-a65d-a47cec815898,
        atns-sub:97be12ad-fd1c-5136-9323-0929eb90b556,
        atns-sub:9c404ff9-19e6-5e64-a8bd-2e3b39773146,
        atns-sub:ffe61b3b-8b29-5264-89ac-758a03928ea5,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=6422> ;
    schema:name "APLNG and Iman People Fairview and Eurombah Creek Projects Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2013-09-04"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the agreement

Commencement

The start date of the Agreement is 4 September 2013. The ILUA was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal on 9 September 2013. No end date is specified but the Agreement is said to come to an end when the agreed acts and the undertaking of the ILUA project finish.

Agreed Acts

The Agreement provides for the parties' consent to certain 'agreed acts' as well as the undertaking of the ILUA project. The Extract specifies these agreed acts in Schedule 2. They are:
- the grant of petroleum authorities related to the undertaking of the ILUA project, including pipeline licences;
- the grant of any other rights and interests, approvals or future acts considerd by APLNG or a third party to be necessary or desirable for or incidental to the undertaking of the ILUA project;
- the undertaking of any acts pursuant to the above grants or acts considered by APLNG or a third party to be necessary or desirable for or incidental to the undertaking of the ILUA project; and
- the making, amendment or repeal of legislation connected to the ILUA project.

Native Title Provisions

Right to negotiate provisions do not apply
The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply, as the alternative consultation provisions are to be followed instead.

Without this agreement, the grant would have been invalid and the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) would apply. Under this Act any activity, such as a grant of land, that may affect native title rights is defined as a ‘future act’ and must comply with the future act provisions of the Act in order to be valid.

Future Acts
The agreed acts include future acts. The Extract notes that the parties' consent to the project and the related agreed acts includes statements of the kind mentioned in ss 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4).

Background to the Agreement:

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Iman People #2 Native Title Claim Group is the registered entity of the Iman People #2 (National Native Title Tribunal File No.: QC97/55).

The ILUA area falls within the Iman People #2 registered native title claim area, which was filed with the Federal Court of Australia as proceeding QUD 6162 of 1998 on 30 October 1997. The claim covers approximately 14,024 square kilometres of land and waters in central and south-western Queensland.

The Iman People #2 native title claim was not accepted for registration on 28 July 1999 due to failing to meet some of the procedural requirements pursuant to the registration test provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth). The claim was, however, later accepted for registration on 26 July 2002 after certain amendments were made.

The claimants in the Iman People #2 native title claim are also party to the Iman #2 and QCG Pty Limited Indigenous Land Use Agreement (National Native Title Tribunal File No. QI2010/003).

The Iman People are currently working with the Queensland Government on a timeline for a consent determination."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/Pages/QLD_-_Registered_ILUA_APLNG_and_Iman_People_Fairview_and_Eurombah_Creek_Projects_ILUA_QI2013_032.aspx"^^xsd:anyURI .

idn-resource:e56b3ed0-4cc8-5adf-8208-c15b5a543f57 a atns:Entity,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    atns:category atns-cat:13e77fec-44fd-554f-a075-ec60788eb1b1 ;
    atns:deleted false ;
    atns:eid "A005892"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "5892"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Jangga/Gunjulla Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA) was agreed between:

- Stratford Pastoral Pty Ltd (applicant); and

- Bulganunna Aboriginal Corporation

on 25 November 2013.

The purpose of this Body Corporate Agreement is to grant consent regarding access to the ILUA Area which is a pastoral property."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:9335b2f1-4915-55cc-9736-2ded7c4a2008,
        atns-sub:bda82010-54a4-5bac-8bf5-4b5341822974,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5892> ;
    schema:name "Jangga/Gunjulla Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:spatialCoverage <https://data.idnau.org/pid/nntt/QI2013-065> ;
    schema:startDate "2013-11-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Details of the Agreement

The ILUA was registered with the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT) on 25 November 2013.

The Extract does not specify specific start or end dates for the Agreement.

However, the Extract does note that the Agreement takes effect on the Date of Determination of Native Title in favour of the Jangga People, being 9 October 2012.

The Agreement will continue in effect until:

(a) the Lease term expires; or
(b) the date of surrender, resumption, forfeiture or termination of the Lease; or
(c) the date upon which the Agreement is removed from the Register of ILUAs.

The Extract does not include extensive information regarding the terms of the Agreement.

Native Title Provisions

The Extract notes that there are no statements within the Agreement of the kind which are mentioned in 24EB(1) or 24EBA(1) or (4) of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth).

This means that the ILUA does not:

- provide consent for the doing of any acts by
non-native title parties;

- effect the right of the native title parties to negotiate with non-native title parties proposing to undertake a future act; nor

- validate any previous future acts.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

On 9 October 2012, the Federal Court of Australia recognised the Jangga People’s Native Title rights and interests over approximately 11,350 square kilometres of land in Central Queensland. The decision of McLennan on behalf of the Jangga People v State of Queensland [2012] FCA 1082 effectively reaffirms the Jangga People’s affinity with their traditional lands around Mount Coolon, Urella and Lake Dalrymple."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/searchRegApps/NativeTitleRegisters/Pages/ILUA_details.aspx?NNTT_Fileno=QI2013/065"^^xsd:anyURI .

