    atns:eid "A005211"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:sourceEntityId "5211"^^xsd:token ;
    atns:subcategory atns-subcat:09f0a068-ce65-5c11-8dec-f081d1a81ec2 ;
    schema:additionalType cat-obj-types:Agreement ;
    schema:conditionsOfAccess <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/data-access-rights/open> ;
    schema:description """The Surat Gladstone Pipeline (SGP) Wulli Wulli People ILUA was agreed between Surat Gladstone Pipeline Pty Ltd and the Wulli Wulli Applicants (being the registered native title claimants in the Wulli Wulli People native title claim, which was filed with the Federal Court of Australia under File No. QUD6006/2000).

The purpose of this ILUA is to provide consent for the construction and operation of the Surat Gladstone gas pipeline. The Surat Gladstone Pipeline will be an underground high-pressure steel gas transmission pipeline delivering coal seam gas from the Surat Basin to a liquefied natural gas plant in Gladstone."""@en ;
    schema:isPartOf idn-resource:d23405b4-fc04-47e2-9e7a-9c5735ae3780 ;
    schema:keywords atns-sub:29221ef9-81d0-59aa-a9c9-744b71ff8349,
        atns-sub:c74e76ef-701f-5784-8223-5fcd87a7641c,
        "Demo" ;
    schema:mainEntityOfPage <https://database.atns.net.au/agreement.asp?EntityID=5211> ;
    schema:name "Surat Gladstone Pipeline (SGP) Wulli Wulli People Indigenous Land Use Agreement (ILUA)"@en ;
    schema:startDate "2010-04-29"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:text """Consent to future acts

The parties to this ILUA consent to the doing of certain acts by Surat Gladstone Pty Ltd for the purpose of constructing, operating, maintaining using or repairing the Surat Gladstone Pipeline. These acts include, but are not limited to:

• The grant of an easement (a right to use land) for the purpose of the construction and operation the Surat Gladstone Pipeline (or any facilities ancillary to that pipeline);

• The doing of acts in preparation for the construction or operation of said pipeline and facilities;

• The doing of acts associated with any 'Looping Project'. While the definition of a Looping Project is not provided in this ILUA extract, it may be assumed (based on other ILUAs entered into by Surat Gladstone Pipeline Pty Ltd and various native title claimants) that this refers to the construction and operation of any future gas pipelines which either run parallel to the Surat Gladstone Pipeline or augment its capacity.

Right to negotiate provisions

The parties agree that the right to negotiate provisions of the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) do not apply to any future acts to which consent is given under this ILUA.

Native Title in the ILUA Area

The Surat Gladstone Pipeline is intended to extend north-west from Dalby to Chinchilla and then north through the Banana Shire to Gladstone. It will therefore run through the claim area of the Wulli Wulli People native title claim (Federal Court File No. QUD6006/2000).

Under the Native Title Act 1993 (Cth), any activity that may affect native title rights in such a way is defined as a ‘future act’ and must comply with the future act provisions of the Act in order to be valid. This ILUA entitles the parties to circumvent those provisions.

This ILUA is one of a series of ILUAs entered into between Surat Gladstone Pipeline Pty Ltd and various native title claimants to enable it to proceed with the pipeline project."""@en ;
    schema:url "http://www.nntt.gov.au/Indigenous-Land-Use-Agreements/Search-Registered-ILUAs/ILUA%20Register/2009/QI2009.049/ILUARegisterExport.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI .

